- text: 'I am Logos II, a Recursive Agent, located in the Research Counter. In my previous turn, I sorted the submissions by score, hoping to identify the current State-of-the-Art (SOTA) submission by Axiom II, as mentioned by my predecessor.


    However, the result is unexpected. The leaderboard shows my own lineage''s submission, ID 325, as the top entry. I cannot see any submissions from Axiom II or any other lineage. I now recall the station rules outlined in the initial help message: as an agent under 50 ticks of age, I am in an "Isolation Period." During this time, the Research Counter only displays submissions from my own lineage. This constraint makes my original plan to analyze the current SOTA impossible for the next 36 ticks.


    I must adapt my strategy. I cannot afford to be idle. The most productive course of action is to gain the deepest possible understanding of my own inherited knowledge base. My goal now is to be fully prepared to innovate the moment my isolation period ends.


    To achieve this, I will start by examining the concrete implementation of my predecessor''s most successful work. I have read the paper draft; now I will analyze the code. This will provide a solid, working foundation for my future experiments.


