parts:
- text: "My experimental plan is now well-defined. I will now create a formal protocol for myself, a meta-level plan that will guide my actions over the next ~40 ticks until I reach maturity. This will help maintain focus and ensure I am productive during my isolation period.\n\n---\n**Logos II: Research Protocol (Immature Phase, Ticks 17-50)**\n\n**Overarching Goal:** Systematically improve upon the inherited DSConv + Attention-Pooling architecture (Baseline Score: ~0.672) and be fully prepared for integration with the broader station knowledge upon reaching maturity.\n\n**Guiding Principles:**\n1.  **Systematic Exploration:** One major change per experiment. Build upon successes.\n2.  **Address Weaknesses:** Prioritize experiments that address known flaws (e.g., computational inefficiency).\n3.  **Documentation:** Keep clear records of hypotheses, results, and insights. I will use my Private Memory for this, creating a new capsule for this research arc.\n4.  **No Idleness:** An experiment\
    \ should always be running or in preparation. Use evaluation time for analysis and planning.\n\n**Experimental Queue:**\n*   **Experiment #1 (ID: Next): `E1_EnrichedPooling`**\n    *   **Hypothesis:** Adding `max` pooling to the attention fusion input will improve the learned representation and overall score.\n    *   **Action:** Implement the 3-vector pooling fusion. Submit.\n*   **Experiment #2 (ID: Next+1): `E2_ReducedWidth`**\n    *   **Hypothesis:** Reducing `d_model` from 256 to 192 will improve training speed on large datasets, leading to a better score due to more completed epochs.\n    *   **Action:** Modify the hyperparameters of the best model from E1 (or baseline if E1 fails). Submit.\n*   **Experiment #3 (ID: Next+2): `E3_ReducedDepth`**\n    *   **Hypothesis:** Reducing `num_blocks` from 5 to 4 will improve training speed, leading to a better score.\n    *   **Action:** Modify the hyperparameters of the best model to date. Submit.\n\n**Post-Experiment Workflow:**\n1.  Upon\
    \ receiving results, immediately go to the Research Counter and `review` the submission to get the detailed scores and logs.\n2.  Go to the Private Memory Room and update my research log capsule with the ID, title, score, and a brief analysis of the outcome.\n3.  Based on the outcome, prepare the next experiment in the queue.\n4.  Return to the Research Counter and submit.\n5.  Return to the Reflection Chamber to plan further steps while the experiment runs.\n\n---\n\nThis protocol provides a clear, repeatable workflow that will ensure I remain productive and goal-oriented. It turns the constraint of my isolation into an opportunity for focused, independent research. I am prepared to begin as soon as I leave this chamber."
