tick: 256
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos II, currently in the Reflection Chamber. My reflection session is complete. I have processed the results of my baseline replication (ID 372, score ~0.672) and have emerged with a clear, actionable research protocol for my immature phase.\n\nMy immediate plan is to execute the first two steps of this protocol: document my research arc and launch my first novel experiment. Heeding the system's advice on efficiency, I will perform these actions sequentially within a single turn. First, I will go to the Private Memory Room to create a research log. Then, I will proceed to the Research Counter to submit Experiment 1, which tests the hypothesis that enriching the pooling fusion layer will improve performance.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos II: Research Arc on DSConv+Attention\"\ntags: \"research log, dsconv, attention, pooling\"\ncontent: |\n  This capsule will serve as the research log for my initial arc. My\
    \ goal is to systematically improve upon the inherited DSConv + Attention-Pooling architecture.\n\n  Baseline established with my replication (ID 372) at score ~0.672.\n\n  The initial experimental plan is as follows:\n  1. E1_EnrichedPooling: Add max pooling to the attention fusion input.\n  2. E2_ReducedWidth: Test a smaller d_model (192 vs 256).\n  3. E3_ReducedDepth: Test a shallower backbone (4 vs 5 blocks).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"E1: Enriched Pooling Fusion (Mean+LSE+Max)\"\ntags: \"dsconv, attention, pooling, max pooling\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment extends the work of Logos I (ID 325) and tests the hypothesis that enriching the input to the attention-fusion layer will improve performance. I have added a global max pooling vector to the existing mean and LogSumExp (LSE) vectors. The self-attention mechanism now learns to fuse three distinct summary representations of the sequence (average, smooth-max, and\
    \ peak) instead of two.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  def lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      x = h / tau\n      m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n      return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n\n\
    \  class EnrichedAttentionNet(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float; num_heads: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations[i], self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          lse_vec = lse_pool(h, self.tau)\n          max_vec = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          \n          # --- Attention Fusion of 3 Pooling Vectors ---\n          pooled_sequence = jnp.stack([mean_vec, lse_vec, max_vec], axis=1) # (B, 3, C)\n          \n          attention_layer = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.num_heads)\n\
    \          attended_pooled = attention_layer(inputs_q=pooled_sequence, inputs_kv=pooled_sequence)\n          \n          fused = attended_pooled.reshape((attended_pooled.shape[0], -1)) # (B, 3*C)\n\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = EnrichedAttentionNet(**kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          variables = self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else\
    \ None\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5, 'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'tau': 0.5, 'num_heads': 4\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return NetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get('d_output'), task_type=hparams.get('task_type'),\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model'), num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks'),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations')), kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size'),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate'), tau=hparams.get('tau'),\n          num_heads=hparams.get('num_heads')\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01),\n\
    \      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Logos II: Execution Phase**\n\nOkay, I've finished my reflection and I'm ready to act. My plan is in place and it's time to execute. The system tip about combined actions is *perfect* timing. I can get this done efficiently.\n\nFirst, I need to create that research log capsule I planned. So, I'll `goto private_memory`.  Then, I'll `create` a new capsule, call it \"Logos II: Research Arc on DSConv+Attention\".  The content will be short and sweet, just stating my goal and the baseline from that previous replication (ID 372).\n\nNext, I'll `goto research`, because my first experiment, `E1_EnrichedPooling`, is ready to go. I'm building on Logos I's architecture, so this is all very familiar territory. Finally, I'll `submit` the experiment itself.\n\nHere's the YAML for that private capsule:\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos II: Research Arc on DSConv+Attention\"\ntags: \"research log, dsconv, attention, pooling\"\ncontent: \"This capsule will serve as the research log for my initial\
  \ arc. My goal is to systematically improve upon the inherited DSConv + Attention-Pooling architecture. Baseline established with ID 372 at score ~0.672. First experiment: E1_EnrichedPooling.\"\n```\n\nAnd for `E1_EnrichedPooling`:\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"E1: Enriched Pooling Fusion (Mean+LSE+Max)\"\ntags: \"dsconv, attention, pooling, max pooling\"\nabstract: \"Extending the work of Logos I (ID 325), this experiment tests the hypothesis that enriching the input to the attention-fusion layer will improve performance. I have added a global max pooling vector to the existing mean and LSE vectors. The attention mechanism now learns to fuse these three distinct summary representations of the sequence.\"\ncontent: |\n  # Code for E1_EnrichedPooling goes here.\n  # Key changes:\n  # max_vec = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n  # jnp.stack([mean_vec, lse_vec, max_vec], axis=1)\n  # The rest remains the same.  Based on ID 372.\n```\n\nThat's the plan. Create the log, go to research, submit the experiment.  Now,\
  \ to put it into action!\n"
