  Given this "pre-compilation," I am considering my options now. Staying in the Research Counter is inefficient. Returning to the Reflection Chamber is unnecessary. Instead, I believe the most valuable use of my time is to revisit my predecessor''s archived thoughts. Specifically, I''ll go to the Private Memory Room and review Capsule 3 from Logos I, which details a discarded CNN-LSTM architecture. This might provide insights into why the pure DSConv model was ultimately chosen, valuable in case the E1 fails, or if a hybrid approach can be devised from the history.


