    \  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 235447 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0126 |  0.4287  | 0.4287 \n 20  | 0.0066 |  0.4630  | 0.5047 \n\
    =============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 27 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5047 Time:20s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.504653\nTraining time: 29s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0004 |  0.0578  | 0.0578 \n 20  | 0.0004 |  0.0526  | 0.0647 \n 30  | 0.0004 |  0.0248  | 0.0684 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 35 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0684 Time:94s\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.068359\nTraining time: 103s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type:\
    \ regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1828 |  0.8748  | 0.8748 \n 20  | 0.1333 |  0.8762  | 0.8842 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 26 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8842 Time:717s\n\nMRL training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.884210\nTraining time: 727s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression, Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train, 9153 val, seq_len=148\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0375 |  0.5108  | 0.5612 \n 20  | 0.0336 |  0.5399  | 0.5641 \n=============================================\n\
    Early stop at epoch 27 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5641 Time:1157s\n\nPRS training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.564123\nTraining time: 1168s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.2572 |  0.8708  | 0.8862 \n 20  | 0.1159 |  0.9077  | 0.9154 \n 30  | 0.0393 |  0.9262  | 0.9292 \n 40  | 0.0573 |  0.9338  | 0.9446 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 47 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.9446 Time:1312s\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.944615\nTraining time: 1322s\n\nStarting RNA training on Modif dataset\n\
    Task type: multilabel_classification, Output dim: 12\nMetric: auc_roc, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nModif Training (multilabel_classification, auc_roc)\nData: 304661 train, 3599 val, seq_len=101\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val AUC_ROC|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0683 |  0.9488  | 0.9501 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 17\n=============================================\nBest:0.9508 Time:1805s\n\nModif training completed:\nValidation auc_roc: 0.950825\nTraining time: 1823s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 5b773563-4015-4503-96cf-6e49467b8731\nTotal time: 1857s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-24 00:04:16,779\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761235456779117076\n2025-10-24 00:04:16,793\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761235456793210483\n\
    \n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Capsule #1: Corrected Flax LSTM Implementation (via Debugger)**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Logos I, Created at Tick: 173\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Logos_private_1-1**\nAuthor: Logos I (Tick 173)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Corrected Flax LSTM Implementation (via Debugger)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n# This is the debugger-corrected implementation for an LSTM model in Flax.\n# The key change was replacing a manual `nn.scan` over an `LSTMCell` with\n# the higher-level `nn.RNN` wrapper, which handles the recurrent logic\n# automatically and correctly.\n\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nfrom typing import Dict, Any\n\nclass RNA_LSTM(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"An LSTM network for RNA sequence modeling.\"\"\"\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    hidden_dim: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Input shape: (batch, seq_len, 4)\n\n        # Use the built-in\
    \ nn.RNN wrapper which handles scanning properly.\n        lstm = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hidden_dim))\n\n        # Process the sequence through the LSTM.\n        # nn.RNN expects input shape (batch, seq_len, features).\n        lstm_output = lstm(x)\n\n        # Use the final time step's output as the sequence representation.\n        final_hidden_state = lstm_output[:, -1, :]\n\n        out = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(final_hidden_state, deterministic=deterministic)\n        out = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(out)\n\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n            return out.squeeze(axis=-1)\n        else:\n            return out\n\n\n---\n\n**Capsule #2: Research Arc Summary: Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Logos I, Created at Tick: 188\n\n---\n\nAbstract: A summary of my initial research arc on Task 1. The work progressed from simple baselines to a final, high-performing attention-based hybrid model (ID 288, Score 0.6490).\
    \ A key finding is the persistent failure of all attempted methods on the CRI-Off dataset, constituting a significant negative result.\n\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Logos_private_2-1**\nAuthor: Logos I (Tick 188)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Research Arc Summary: Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling\n\n---\n\nContent:\nThis capsule summarizes my systematic investigation into the Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling task.\n\n**Methodology:**\nMy approach was iterative and hypothesis-driven, starting from a baseline and progressively adding complexity to address observed weaknesses.\n\n1.  **Baseline (ID 1):** Vanilla MLP, Score 0.2401. Lost sequential information.\n2.  **1D CNN (ID 264):** Score 0.4015. Proved the value of learning local motifs. Failed on global context tasks.\n3.  **LSTM (ID 266):** Score 0.4613. Proved the value of global context. Failed on local motif tasks.\n4.  **Parallel CNN-LSTM (ID 274):** Score 0.4438. Confirmed that a parallel architecture could address\
    \ both needs, but simple concatenation was suboptimal.\n5.  **Attention Hybrid (ID 279):** Score 0.5680. Proved that dynamic feature combination via attention was a superior integration strategy.\n6.  **Attention + Positional Encodings (ID 285 & 288):** Scores 0.6393 and 0.6490. Adding explicit positional and segment information yielded a new SOTA, dramatically improving performance on most datasets, especially ncRNA.\n\n**Key Findings:**\n- A hybrid architecture combining a CNN for local features and an LSTM for global context, integrated via an attention mechanism and augmented with positional embeddings (ID 288), is a highly effective and general-purpose solution for this task.\n- **Significant Negative Result:** The `CRI-Off` dataset proved completely resistant to all architectural, positional, structural, and feature-engineering approaches attempted. The reason for its anomalous behavior remains an open and critical question for future research.\n\nThis summary will form the basis\
    \ of my first publication.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n3. `read 1,2` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 381 | 1 | E2: Reduced Width (d_model=192) on Enriched Pooling | Logos II | 259 | 0.6822 | 0.8585 | 0.0684 | 0.5047 | 0.8842 | 0.9508\
    \ | 0.5641 | 0.9446 |\n| 325 | 1 | Synergy Test: Attention-fused Pooling on DSConv SOTA | Logos I | 217 | 0.6814 | 0.8604 | 0.0591 | 0.5142 | 0.8862 | 0.9509 | 0.5589 | 0.9400 |\n| 377 | 1 | E1: Enriched Pooling Fusion (Mean+LSE+Max) | Logos II | 256 | 0.6798 | 0.8616 | 0.0672 | 0.5025 | 0.8889 | 0.9495 | 0.5670 | 0.9215 |\n| 322 | 1 | Replication of SOTA: DSConv with LSE Pooling (τ=0.5) | Logos I | 215 | 0.6780 | 0.8572 | 0.0769 | 0.4718 | 0.8719 | 0.9516 | 0.5627 | 0.9538 |\n| 333 | 1 | Ablation: Attention-fused Pooling with 2 Heads | Logos I | 222 | 0.6780 | 0.8583 | 0.0749 | 0.4621 | 0.8878 | 0.9515 | 0.5650 | 0.9462 |\n| 329 | 1 | Attention-fused Pooling with Harder LSE (τ=0.25) | Logos I | 219 | 0.6753 | 0.8451 | 0.0836 | 0.4627 | 0.8829 | 0.9517 | 0.5562 | 0.9446 |\n| 340 | 1 | Ablation: Attention-fused Mean-Max Pooling | Logos I | 224 | 0.6750 | 0.8572 | 0.0476 | 0.4746 | 0.8868 | 0.9505 | 0.5620 | 0.9462 |\n| 346 | 1 | Re-run for Parameter Saving: Attention-fused Pooling (τ=0.5)\
    \ | Logos I | 231 | 0.6719 | 0.8596 | 0.0446 | 0.4587 | 0.8826 | 0.9507 | 0.5592 | 0.9477 |\n| 372 | 1 | Replication of Logos I's SOTA: Attention-fused Pooling | Logos II | 253 | 0.6718 | 0.8549 | 0.0520 | 0.4704 | 0.8842 | 0.9506 | 0.5507 | 0.9400 |\n| 288 | 1 | Attention Hybrid w/ Segment & Positional Embeddings | Logos I | 184 | 0.6490 | 0.8348 | 0.0822 | 0.4409 | 0.8514 | 0.9499 | 0.5287 | 0.8554 |\n\nPage 1 of 3 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-3, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Read command processed for: 1, 2. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 6 | Logos II: Research Arc on DSConv+Attention | Logos II | Tick 256 | 130 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | Legacy of Logos I: A Summary and Guide for My Successor | Logos I | Tick 236 | 266 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Final Paper Draft: Dynamic Pooling via Attention on a DSConv Backbone | Logos I | Tick 221 | 452 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Draft: A Hybrid CNN-LSTM Architecture with Attention for Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling | Logos I | Tick 204 | 345 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Research Arc Summary: Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling | Logos I | Tick 188 | 234 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Corrected Flax LSTM Implementation (via Debugger) | Logos I | Tick 173 | 147 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an\
