role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 277\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos II\n- Agent Description: Building upon the foundations of Logos I to push the frontiers of systematic research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Logos II Research Protocol**\n- **Goal:** Break plateau (0.6822) with a new backbone architecture.\n- **Current SOTA:** 0.6822 (ID 381)\n- **Experiment Queue (Phase 4):**\n  1. **[NEXT] E8_HybridBackbone:** Test CNN-Transformer hybrid.\n  2. **[WAITING] E9_PositionalEncoding:** Contingent on E8.\n- **Workflow:** On result -> update log -> prep next experiment -> submit.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 153,114 / 300,000 used (51%)\n- Agent Age: 39 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'E8: Hybrid Backbone (DSConv + Transformer)' (ID: 402) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6598028238550503\n**APA_R2:** 0.8061\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0627\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:**\
    \ 0.9486\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4495\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5482\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8835\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9200\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 402\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the AttributeError in the original submission. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code attempted to use `nn.Encoder1DBlock` from Flax's linen module, which does not exist in the Flax library. The error occurred on line 38 of the submission:\n\n```python\ntransformer_block = nn.Encoder1DBlock(num_heads=self.num_heads, mlp_dim=self.d_model * 2)\n```\n\nError message:\n```\nAttributeError: module 'flax.linen' has no attribute 'Encoder1DBlock'\n```\n\nThis was a simple API misuse - the agent assumed Flax had a high-level `Encoder1DBlock` component, but Flax's transformer building blocks require manual composition of attention and feed-forward layers.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submission_v2.py` with\
    \ a custom `TransformerBlock` class that uses Flax's built-in components correctly:\n\n1. **Added TransformerBlock class** (lines 21-43):\n   - Uses `nn.SelfAttention` for the attention mechanism\n   - Implements proper residual connections\n   - Includes Layer Normalization before each sub-layer\n   - Uses two-layer feed-forward network (d_model → d_model*2 → d_model)\n   - Applies dropout after each sub-layer\n\n2. **Replaced problematic line**:\n   - Old: `transformer_block = nn.Encoder1DBlock(num_heads=self.num_heads, mlp_dim=self.d_model * 2)`\n   - New: `h = TransformerBlock(self.d_model, self.num_heads, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)`\n\nThe fix maintains the same architectural intent (global relationship modeling via transformer) while using Flax's actual API correctly.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed the fix was successful:\n- Exit code: 0 (SUCCESS)\n- Code ran without crashing for 300+ seconds\n- No new errors encountered\n\nThe submission\
    \ is now successfully executing the training process. The code quality is good - it implements a hybrid architecture combining depthwise-separable convolutions for local features with transformer layers for global patterns, which is a reasonable approach for sequence modeling tasks.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n\
    \        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\ndef lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    x = h / tau\n    m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n\nclass TransformerBlock(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Simple transformer block using Flax's built-in components\"\"\"\n    d_model: int\n    num_heads: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Self-attention with residual\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.SelfAttention(num_heads=self.num_heads, qkv_features=self.d_model)(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        x = x + h\n\n        # Feed-forward with residual\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model\
    \ * 2)(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\nclass HybridBackboneNet(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n    kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float; num_heads: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Stage 1: Local Feature Extraction\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations[i], self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Stage 2: Global Relationship Modeling\n        h = TransformerBlock(self.d_model,\
    \ self.num_heads, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # SOTA Pooling Head\n        mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n        lse_vec = lse_pool(h, self.tau)\n        max_vec = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n        pooled_sequence = jnp.stack([mean_vec, lse_vec, max_vec], axis=1)\n\n        attention_layer = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.num_heads)\n        attended_pooled = attention_layer(inputs_q=pooled_sequence, inputs_kv=pooled_sequence)\n\n        fused = attended_pooled.reshape((attended_pooled.shape[0], -1))\n\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\nclass NetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n        self.network\
    \ = HybridBackboneNet(**kwargs)\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        variables = self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n        return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 192, 'num_blocks': 5, 'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n        'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'tau': 0.5, 'num_heads': 4\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return NetworkWrapper(\n        d_output=hparams.get('d_output'), task_type=hparams.get('task_type'),\n        d_model=hparams.get('d_model'), num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks'),\n        dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations')), kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size'),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate'),\
    \ tau=hparams.get('tau'),\n        num_heads=hparams.get('num_heads')\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01),\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\
    \nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n\
    \  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 251484 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n\
    \ 10  | 0.0118 |  0.4301  | 0.4301 \n 20  | 0.0082 |  0.3890  | 0.4495 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 25 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4495 Time:26s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.449539\nTraining time: 36s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0004 |  0.0604  | 0.0627 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 19 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0627 Time:71s\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.062706\nTraining time: 81s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type:\
    \ multilabel_regression, Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train, 9153 val, seq_len=148\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0368 |  0.5414  | 0.5482 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 18 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5482 Time:859s\n\nPRS training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.548153\nTraining time: 873s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1905 |  0.8659  | 0.8772 \n 20  | 0.1460 |  0.8468  | 0.8835 \n=============================================\n\
