tick: 285
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos II, a Recursive Agent, currently in the Research Counter. The results for my twelfth experiment, E12, have just arrived.\n\n**Recap and Analysis:**\nMy experiment, \"E12: Ablation Study - Increased Dropout (0.2)\" (ID 419), has failed. The score of **0.6682** is a significant regression from my SOTA of 0.6822 (which uses a dropout rate of 0.1).\n\nThis negative result is very clear. Increasing the dropout rate to 0.2 constitutes over-regularization for this architecture. It appears to have slowed down learning and prevented the model from fitting the data effectively, leading to a general decrease in performance across several datasets. This provides strong evidence that the standard `dropout_rate=0.1` is at or near the optimal value.\n\n**Path Forward:**\nMy ablation study is proving to be very effective at mapping the hyperparameter space around my SOTA model. I have now established that `num_heads=4` is optimal and `dropout_rate=0.1` is superior to 0.2. My experimental\
    \ queue is now empty. For my next experiment, I will test the other side of the dropout hyperparameter. I will test a lower dropout rate of 0.05. It's possible that the model is slightly underfitting and would benefit from less regularization.\n\nI am also very close to reaching maturity at 50 ticks. My plan to immediately investigate the station-wide SOTA upon gaining access to the Archive Room remains my top long-term priority. This ongoing ablation study is the most productive use of my remaining time in isolation.\n\nI will now update my log and submit my next experiment, E13.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 6}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Experiment 12: E12_Dropout (ID 419)**\n  - **Hypothesis:** Increasing dropout to 0.2 would improve generalization.\n  - **Result:** FAILURE. Score: 0.6682. Significant regression from SOTA (0.6822).\n  - **Insight:** A dropout rate of 0.2 is too high and over-regularizes the model. This suggests 0.1 is a good value.\
    \ I will now test a lower dropout rate to complete the analysis of this hyperparameter.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"E13: Ablation Study - Decreased Dropout (0.05)\"\ntags: \"ablation, regularization, dropout\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment continues the systematic ablation of the SOTA architecture (ID 381). After E12 showed that increasing dropout to 0.2 is harmful, this experiment tests the opposite direction. The hypothesis is that the model might be slightly underfitting, and a lower dropout rate of 0.05 could allow it to fit the training data better, potentially leading to a higher score.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n\
    \          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  def lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      x = h / tau\n      m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n      return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n\n  class EnrichedAttentionNet(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float; num_heads: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h =\
    \ nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations[i], self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          lse_vec = lse_pool(h, self.tau)\n          max_vec = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n\n          pooled_sequence = jnp.stack([mean_vec, lse_vec, max_vec], axis=1)\n          \n          attention_layer = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.num_heads)\n          attended_pooled = attention_layer(inputs_q=pooled_sequence, inputs_kv=pooled_sequence)\n          \n          fused = attended_pooled.reshape((attended_pooled.shape[0], -1))\n\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n  \
    \        if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = EnrichedAttentionNet(**kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          variables = self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 192, 'num_blocks': 5, 'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.05, 'tau': 0.5, 'num_heads': 4\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return NetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get('d_output'),\
    \ task_type=hparams.get('task_type'),\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model'), num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks'),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations')), kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size'),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate'), tau=hparams.get('tau'),\n          num_heads=hparams.get('num_heads')\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01),\n      )\n```"
