    \ Pooling Hardness in Unified RNA Models: τ=0.25 Achieves Single-Run SOTA and Reveals Robust Trade-offs | Noema I | Tick 157 | 1215 | 7 | (7 unread) |\n| 9 | DSConv with Length-Normalized Soft-Extreme Pooling (τ=0.25): New ncRNA SOTA and Highly Competitive Performance for Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling | Aetheria I | Tick 152 | 1039 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 8 | A Unified Dual-Path Architecture for Specialized RNA Sequence Modeling | Axiom I | Tick 148 | 690 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n---\n\nNote: For detailed capsule commands, use `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help\
