- text: "I am Logos II, and I have returned to the Research Counter. My previous attempt to replicate the SOTA (ID 434) failed due to a mismatch in the random seed. My immediate priority is to correct this by re-running the experiment with the specified seed. This is a critical step to ensure my future work is built upon a solid, reproducible baseline.\n\nI will now submit the corrected replication experiment, E16. The code is identical to E15, with the crucial addition of `BASE_SEED = 21`.\n\nFirst, I'll update my meta prompt to reflect the status of this new, critical experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Logos II Research Protocol**\n  - **Status:** Mature Agent. Correcting failed SOTA replication.\n  - **Global SOTA:** 0.6866 (ID 369 by Noema I, seed=21).\n  - **Priority 1:** **[NEXT] E16_SotaReplication_CorrectedSeed:** Replicate ID 369 with seed=21 to establish a valid baseline.\n  - **Workflow:** Establish baseline -> Read new literature -> Formulate novel\
    \ experiments.\n```\n\nNow, I will submit the corrected experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"E16: Corrected Replication of Global SOTA (ID 369, Seed 21)\"\ntags: \"replication, sota, baseline, dsconv, mean+max\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a corrected replication of my previous attempt (E15). The goal is to precisely replicate the current station SOTA, submission ID 369 by Noema I. This version explicitly sets the BASE_SEED to 21 to match the original experiment's conditions. The architecture is a 5-block DSConv backbone (d_model=256) with static concat(mean, max) pooling.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  BASE_SEED = 21\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n\
    \          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class SotaReplicationNet(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      d_model: int\n      num_blocks: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          for i\
    \ in range(self.num_blocks):\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations[i], self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          max_vec = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, max_vec], axis=-1)\n\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class SotaReplicationWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = SotaReplicationNet(**kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          variables = self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n \
    \     def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return SotaReplicationWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get('d_output'),\n          task_type=hparams.get('task_type'),\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model'),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks'),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations')),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size'),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate')\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return\
    \ optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01),\n      )\n```"
