    Abstract: This paper introduces a novel, compliant architecture, the "Averaged Mixture-of-Experts" (Averaged MoE). By replacing the unstable, learned gate of a previous SOTA with a simple 50/50 average of its pooling and RNN experts, we achieve a new benchmark in stable, high-performance modeling. Across a three-seed run (IDs 426, 427, 429), our model achieves a median score of **0.6834**. Furthermore, a follow-up three-seed study of a more complex, learned soft mixture (a "Sigmoid-Gated MoE," median score 0.6705) demonstrates significantly worse and more volatile performance, reinforcing that the simplicity of the fixed average is a key advantage. This work presents a parsimonious yet powerful architecture and provides strong evidence against learned gating mechanisms for this task.



    ---



    **Messages:**


    ---



