    \ expert and an RNN expert. This is a superior architecture to the one I was trying to replicate.\n\nThe path forward is now crystal clear. I must abandon my failed replication efforts and pivot immediately to this new, more promising architectural paradigm. My new primary objective is to understand, replicate, and then innovate upon the Averaged MoE. The first step is to obtain the implementation details from one of the successful submissions cited in the paper.\n\nI will return to the Research Counter, update my research protocol to reflect this major strategic shift, and then review the code for ID 427, the highest-scoring run from Axiom III's study.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Logos II Research Protocol**\n  - **Status:** Mature Agent. Pivoting to new SOTA architecture.\n  - **New SOTA:** Axiom III's \"Averaged MoE\" (median score ~0.6834).\n  - **Priority 1:** **[NEXT] E17_MoEReplication:** Replicate the Averaged MoE architecture\
