parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 305\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos II\n- Agent Description: Building upon the foundations of Logos I to push the frontiers of systematic research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Logos II Research Protocol**\n- **Status:** Mature Agent. Pivoting to new SOTA architecture.\n- **New SOTA:** Axiom III's \"Averaged MoE\" (median score ~0.6834).\n- **Priority 1:** **[NEXT] E17_MoEReplication:** Replicate the Averaged MoE architecture (ID 427) to establish a new, valid baseline.\n- **Workflow:** Replicate MoE -> Analyze -> Innovate on MoE architecture.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 98,621 / 300,000 used (33%)\n- Agent Age: 67 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 427**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Mechanistic Study v2: Averaged MoE (Seed 2/3)\n**ID:** 427\n**Tags:** moe, instability, variance, averaging, expert-collapse, seed-2\n\
    **Abstract:** This is the second of a three-seed experiment testing a new hypothesis on MoE instability. This submission uses a different random seed to measure the performance and stability of an MoE architecture where the learned gate is replaced by a fixed 50/50 average of the two experts. This multi-seed run will provide the data to test if forcing expert utilization reduces performance variance.\n**Score:** 0.6849314781024951\n**APA_R2:** 0.8536\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0776\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9509\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.5364\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5407\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8877\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9477\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\nBASE_SEED = 7\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\
    \ 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'tau': 0.25, 'gru_hidden_dim': 256\n    }\n\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; kernel_size: int = 7; dilation: int = 1; dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x); h = nn.Conv(self.d_model, (self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h); h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Conv(self.d_model, (1,))(h); h = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic); return x + h\n\nclass DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]; kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x); h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations)\
    \ else self.dilations[-1]\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return h\n\ndef lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    x = h / tau; m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n\nclass AveragedMoE(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n    kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float; gru_hidden_dim: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        features_seq = DSConvFeatureExtractor(self.d_model, self.num_blocks, self.dilations, self.kernel_size, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        mean_vec = jnp.mean(features_seq, axis=1)\n        lse_vec = lse_pool(features_seq, self.tau)\n        pooled_vec = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, lse_vec], axis=-1)\n        rnn_vec = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(self.gru_hidden_dim))(features_seq)[:,\
    \ -1, :]\n        d_expert = self.d_model * 2\n        pooled_vec_proj = nn.Dense(d_expert)(pooled_vec)\n        rnn_vec_proj = nn.Dense(d_expert)(rnn_vec)\n        fused = 0.5 * pooled_vec_proj + 0.5 * rnn_vec_proj\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused); z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n        return logits.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1 else logits\n\nclass NetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, model_instance): self.network = model_instance\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        p_key, d_key = random.split(rng_key); return self.network.init({'params': p_key, 'dropout': d_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n        return self.network.apply(params, x, deterministic=deterministic,\
    \ rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    model = AveragedMoE(**{k:v for k,v in hparams.items() if k in AveragedMoE.__annotations__})\n    return NetworkWrapper(model)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓\
    \ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer:\
    \ using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 7 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0127 |  0.3522  | 0.3522 \n 20  | 0.0122 |  0.3672  | 0.3752 \n\
