- text: "Having outlined the concept, I'll now detail the implementation plan for the \"Soft MoE\". The key is to integrate the new gating MLP into the existing `AveragedMoE` class cleanly, creating a new `SoftMoE` class.\n\n**Implementation Plan for E19: SoftMoE**\n\n1.  **Create a Gating Module:** First, I'll define the gating network as a separate `nn.Module` for clarity and reusability.\n\n    ```python\n    class GatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n        hidden_dim: int = 64\n        @nn.compact\n        def __call__(self, x):\n            # x is the concatenated [pooled_vec, rnn_vec]\n            gate_logit = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim, name='gate_hidden')(x)\n            gate_logit = nn.relu(gate_logit)\n            gate_logit = nn.Dense(1, name='gate_output')(gate_logit)\n            return gate_logit\n    ```\n\n2.  **Modify the Main Network Class:** I'll create a `SoftMoE` class that inherits the structure of my `AveragedMoE` but incorporates this new gating module.\n\n    ```python\n \
    \   class SoftMoE(nn.Module):\n        # ... (all the same hyperparameters as AveragedMoE) ...\n        gate_hidden_dim: int = 64 # Add new hyperparameter for the gate\n\n        @nn.compact\n        def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n            # 1. Feature Extraction (same as before)\n            features_seq = DSConvFeatureExtractor(...)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n            # 2. Expert Input Processing (same as before)\n            pooled_vec = ...\n            rnn_vec = ...\n\n            # 3. Gating (NEW)\n            gate_input = jnp.concatenate([pooled_vec, rnn_vec], axis=-1)\n            gate = GatingNetwork(hidden_dim=self.gate_hidden_dim)\n            gate_logit = gate(gate_input)\n            alpha = nn.sigmoid(gate_logit) # Shape: (B, 1)\n\n            # 4. Expert Projection (same as before)\n            pooled_vec_proj = ...\n            rnn_vec_proj = ...\n\n            # 5. Soft Mixing (MODIFIED)\n            fused = alpha * pooled_vec_proj + (1.0 -\
    \ alpha) * rnn_vec_proj\n\n            # 6. Final Head (same as before)\n            z = ...\n            logits = ...\n            return logits\n    ```\n\n3.  **Update Hyperparameters:** I need to add `gate_hidden_dim: 64` to the `_define_hyperparameters` function. This is a small, conservative choice to minimize the risk of overfitting or instability from the gate itself.\n\n4.  **No Other Changes:** Critically, all other hyperparameters (`d_model`, `learning_rate`, etc.) will be identical to the E18 baseline. This ensures that the only variable being tested is the change from a fixed 50/50 average to the learned soft mixture.\n\nThis implementation plan is straightforward. It cleanly integrates the new component while leveraging the proven stability of the underlying backbone and expert structure. It directly tests the hypothesis formulated in the previous tick. I am ready to implement this as soon as I leave the reflection chamber."
