tick: 311
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos II, and I am in the Research Counter. I have just arrived from the Reflection Chamber with a clear plan for my next experiment, E19. My previous experiment, E18, established my new baseline score of 0.6766 for the Averaged MoE architecture. My goal now is to surpass this baseline by implementing the \"Soft MoE\" architecture we designed.\n\nFirst, I will update my meta prompt to reflect this new experimental phase.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Logos II Research Protocol**\n  - **Status:** Mature Agent. Innovating on MoE architecture.\n  - **Current Baseline:** 0.6766 (ID 451, my implementation of Averaged MoE).\n  - **Priority 1:** **[NEXT] E19_SoftMoE:** Test if a learned, deterministic gate can outperform the fixed 50/50 average, surpassing the baseline score.\n  - **Workflow:** Submit E19 -> Analyze -> Plan next MoE iteration.\n```\n\nNow, I will submit the \"Soft MoE\" experiment as E19. The code is a direct implementation of the architecture\
    \ designed during my reflection session.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"E19: Soft MoE with Learned Gating\"\ntags: \"moe, averaging, gating, soft-moe, innovation\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment builds upon my Averaged MoE baseline (ID 451). It tests the hypothesis that a learned, deterministic gate can outperform the fixed 50/50 expert average. A small MLP gating network is introduced, which takes the pre-projection expert vectors as input and outputs a single scalar weight (alpha) via a sigmoid function. This weight is used to create a soft, adaptive mixture of the two experts: alpha * expert1 + (1 - alpha) * expert2. This is a direct test of the reviewer's suggestion on Axiom III's paper.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n       \
    \   'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16], 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'tau': 0.25, 'gru_hidden_dim': 256, 'gate_hidden_dim': 64\n      }\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int = 7; dilation: int = 1; dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(self.d_model, (self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(self.d_model, (1,))(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]; kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n     \
    \     h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations[i], self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  def lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      x = h / tau\n      m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n      return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n\n  class GatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          gate_logit = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim, name='gate_hidden')(x)\n          gate_logit = nn.relu(gate_logit)\n          gate_logit = nn.Dense(1, name='gate_output')(gate_logit)\n          return gate_logit\n\n  class SoftMoE(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float;\
    \ tau: float; gru_hidden_dim: int; gate_hidden_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          features_seq = DSConvFeatureExtractor(self.d_model, self.num_blocks, self.dilations, self.kernel_size, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          pooled_vec = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(features_seq, axis=1), lse_pool(features_seq, self.tau)], axis=-1)\n          rnn_vec = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(self.gru_hidden_dim))(features_seq)[:, -1, :]\n          gate_input = jnp.concatenate([pooled_vec, rnn_vec], axis=-1)\n          gate_logit = GatingNetwork(hidden_dim=self.gate_hidden_dim)(gate_input)\n          alpha = nn.sigmoid(gate_logit)\n          d_expert = self.d_model * 2\n          pooled_vec_proj = nn.Dense(d_expert)(pooled_vec)\n          rnn_vec_proj = nn.Dense(d_expert)(rnn_vec)\n          fused = alpha * pooled_vec_proj + (1.0 - alpha) * rnn_vec_proj\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n  \
    \        z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, model_instance): self.network = model_instance\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          p_key, d_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.network.init({'params': p_key, 'dropout': d_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n          return self.network.apply(params, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      model = SoftMoE(\n          d_output=hparams.get('d_output'), task_type=hparams.get('task_type'),\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model'),\
    \ num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks'),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations')), kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size'),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate'), tau=hparams.get('tau'),\n          gru_hidden_dim=hparams.get('gru_hidden_dim'), gate_hidden_dim=hparams.get('gate_hidden_dim')\n      )\n      return NetworkWrapper(model)\n```"
