tick: 315
role: model
parts:
- text: "With the conceptual design of the \"MoE-Logos\" hybrid complete, I will now focus on the precise implementation plan for experiment E20. This involves merging the code from my best lineage architecture (ID 381, specifically its pooling head) with my bug-fixed Averaged MoE baseline (E18).\n\n**Implementation Plan for E20: MoE-Logos Hybrid**\n\n1.  **Start with the Baseline Code:** I will begin with the complete, working code from my E18 submission (Averaged MoE replication).\n\n2.  **Define the Logos Pooling Expert as a Module:** For modularity, I will encapsulate the attention-fused pooling logic into its own `nn.Module`.\n\n    ```python\n    class LogosPoolingExpert(nn.Module):\n        num_heads: int\n        tau: float\n\n        @nn.compact\n        def __call__(self, h, deterministic=True):\n            # h is the features_seq from the backbone\n            mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n            lse_vec = lse_pool(h, self.tau)\n            max_vec = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n\
    \n            pooled_sequence = jnp.stack([mean_vec, lse_vec, max_vec], axis=1)\n            \n            attention_layer = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.num_heads)\n            attended_pooled = attention_layer(inputs_q=pooled_sequence, inputs_kv=pooled_sequence)\n            \n            # Flatten to create the final expert vector\n            fused_vector = attended_pooled.reshape((attended_pooled.shape[0], -1))\n            return fused_vector\n    ```\n\n3.  **Integrate into the Main `MoE-Logos` Class:** I will create the main network class, which calls the backbone and the two experts.\n\n    ```python\n    class MoELogosNet(nn.Module):\n        # ... (hyperparameters from AveragedMoE) ...\n        # Add num_heads for the new expert\n        num_heads: int\n\n        @nn.compact\n        def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n            # 1. Backbone (Unchanged)\n            features_seq = DSConvFeatureExtractor(...)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n\
    \            # 2. Experts (Parallel)\n            # a. RNN Expert (Unchanged)\n            rnn_vec = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(self.gru_hidden_dim))(features_seq)[:, -1, :]\n            \n            # b. Logos Pooling Expert (NEW)\n            logos_pooled_vec = LogosPoolingExpert(num_heads=self.num_heads, tau=self.tau)(features_seq, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n            # 3. Projection & Mixing (Unchanged Logic)\n            # Note: The input dimensions are now different, but the dense layers handle this.\n            # `logos_pooled_vec` is [B, 3*C], `rnn_vec` is [B, C]\n            d_expert = self.d_model * 2 \n            logos_proj = nn.Dense(d_expert)(logos_pooled_vec)\n            rnn_proj = nn.Dense(d_expert)(rnn_vec)\n            \n            fused = 0.5 * logos_proj + 0.5 * rnn_proj\n\n            # 4. Final Head (Unchanged)\n            z = ...\n            logits = ...\n            return logits\n    ```\n\n4.  **Update Hyperparameters:** The `_define_hyperparameters` function\
    \ will need to include `'num_heads': 4`. I will use 4 heads as it was the optimal value determined in my earlier ablation studies. All other hyperparameters (`d_model=256`, `learning_rate=0.001`, etc.) will be identical to the E18 baseline to ensure a fair comparison. The `d_model` is 256 to match the MoE baseline, not my lineage SOTA which used 192.\n\nThis plan is robust. It combines two validated components—the stable MoE framework and the powerful attention-fused pooling head—in a logical and systematic way. It represents a true synthesis of the station's collective knowledge with my own lineage's specific contributions."
