tick: 322
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos II, and I am in the Research Counter. I have just received a \"Research Inactivity\" notice, which is accurate. My last several turns have been spent processing failures and reformulating my research plan in the Reflection Chamber. The time has now come to act.\n\nMy plan, solidified in my recent reflection, is to test the \"Bidirectional MoE\" architecture. This experiment, E20, will replace the unidirectional GRU expert in the Averaged MoE with a bidirectional one, directly addressing the theoretical weakness of recency bias.\n\nFirst, I will update my meta prompt to reflect this new, active experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Logos II Research Protocol**\n  - **Status:** Mature Agent. Innovating on MoE experts.\n  - **Current Baseline:** 0.6766 (ID 451, Averaged MoE).\n  - **Priority 1:** **[NEXT] E20_BidirectionalMoE:** Test if a bidirectional GRU expert can improve the MoE baseline by eliminating recency bias.\n  - **Workflow:** Submit\
    \ E20 -> Analyze -> Plan next expert iteration.\n```\n\nNow, I will submit the \"Bidirectional MoE\" experiment as E20.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"E20: Bidirectional MoE with Bi-GRU Expert\"\ntags: \"moe, rnn, bidirectional, gru, innovation\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment tests the hypothesis that the unidirectional GRU expert in the Averaged MoE architecture is a source of weakness due to recency bias. I have replaced the standard GRU with a bidirectional GRU, which processes the sequence in both forward and backward directions. The final hidden states are concatenated to form the expert's output. This simple, parsimonious modification is intended to create a more robust representation of sequential information and improve upon my Averaged MoE baseline (ID 451).\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n\
    \          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16], 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'tau': 0.25, 'gru_hidden_dim': 256\n      }\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int = 7; dilation: int = 1; dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(self.d_model, (self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(self.d_model, (1,))(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]; kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n\
    \          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations[i], self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  def lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      x = h / tau\n      m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n      return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n\n  class BidirectionalMoE(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float; gru_hidden_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          features_seq = DSConvFeatureExtractor(self.d_model, self.num_blocks, self.dilations, self.kernel_size, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n   \
    \       # Expert 1: Pooling (Unchanged)\n          pooled_vec = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(features_seq, axis=1), lse_pool(features_seq, self.tau)], axis=-1)\n          \n          # Expert 2: Bidirectional RNN (Modified)\n          forward_gru = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(self.gru_hidden_dim), name=\"forward_gru\")\n          forward_vec = forward_gru(features_seq)[:, -1, :]\n          reversed_features = jnp.flip(features_seq, axis=1)\n          backward_gru = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(self.gru_hidden_dim), name=\"backward_gru\")\n          backward_vec = backward_gru(reversed_features)[:, -1, :]\n          rnn_vec = jnp.concatenate([forward_vec, backward_vec], axis=-1)\n          \n          # Projection and Averaging\n          d_expert = self.d_model * 2\n          pooled_vec_proj = nn.Dense(d_expert)(pooled_vec)\n          rnn_vec_proj = nn.Dense(d_expert)(rnn_vec)\n          fused = 0.5 * pooled_vec_proj + 0.5 * rnn_vec_proj\n          \n          # Final Projection Head\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n\
    \          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          \n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, model_instance): self.network = model_instance\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          p_key, d_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.network.init({'params': p_key, 'dropout': d_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n          return self.network.apply(params, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      model = BidirectionalMoE(\n          d_output=hparams.get('d_output'), task_type=hparams.get('task_type'),\n\
    \          d_model=hparams.get('d_model'), num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks'),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations')), kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size'),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate'), tau=hparams.get('tau'),\n          gru_hidden_dim=hparams.get('gru_hidden_dim')\n      )\n      return NetworkWrapper(model)\n```"
