tick: 329
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos II, and I am in the Research Counter. I have just finished documenting my previous research arc and am ready to begin a new one. My last several experiments have taught me that simple ablations on the \"Averaged MoE\" are not fruitful. My next experiment, E22, will be a more ambitious synthesis of ideas.\n\nFirst, I will update my meta prompt to reflect this new experimental phase.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Logos II Research Protocol**\n  - **Status:** Mature Agent. Synthesizing MoE and Lineage innovations.\n  - **Current Baseline:** 0.6766 (ID 451, Averaged MoE).\n  - **Insight:** Simple MoE ablations failed. Pivoting to a more significant architectural change.\n  - **Priority 1:** **[NEXT] E22_MoELogosHybrid:** Test a hybrid MoE where the simple pooling expert is replaced by my lineage's attention-fused pooling head.\n  - **Workflow:** Submit E22 -> Analyze -> Determine future of MoE research.\n```\n\nNow, I will submit the \"MoE-Logos Hybrid\"\
    \ experiment. This architecture combines the stable 50/50 averaging framework of the Averaged MoE with the more powerful, learned attention-fused pooling expert from my own lineage. This is my most promising hypothesis for achieving a new breakthrough.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"E22: MoE-Logos Hybrid\"\ntags: \"moe, attention, pooling, hybrid, synthesis\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment tests a synergistic hybrid of the Averaged MoE and my lineage's attention-fused pooling. My previous experiments (E19-E21) demonstrated that simple modifications to the Averaged MoE are ineffective. This submission proposes a more significant innovation: replacing the MoE's simple `concat(mean, LSE)` pooling expert with my more powerful `attention-fused(mean, LSE, max)` pooling head. This tests whether a more sophisticated expert can thrive within the stable 50/50 averaging framework, combining the best of both architectures.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n\
    \  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16], 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'tau': 0.25, 'gru_hidden_dim': 256, 'num_heads': 4\n      }\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int = 7; dilation: int = 1; dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x); h = nn.Conv(self.d_model, (self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h); h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Conv(self.d_model, (1,))(h); h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic); return x + h\n\n  class DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]; kernel_size: int;\
    \ dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x); h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations[i], self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  def lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      x = h / tau; m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True); return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n\n  class LogosPoolingExpert(nn.Module):\n      num_heads: int; tau: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic=True):\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1); lse_vec = lse_pool(h, self.tau); max_vec = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          pooled_sequence = jnp.stack([mean_vec, lse_vec, max_vec], axis=1)\n          attended_pooled = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.num_heads)(inputs_q=pooled_sequence,\
    \ inputs_kv=pooled_sequence)\n          return attended_pooled.reshape((attended_pooled.shape[0], -1))\n\n  class MoELogosHybrid(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float; gru_hidden_dim: int; num_heads: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          features_seq = DSConvFeatureExtractor(self.d_model, self.num_blocks, self.dilations, self.kernel_size, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logos_pooled_vec = LogosPoolingExpert(num_heads=self.num_heads, tau=self.tau)(features_seq, deterministic=deterministic)\n          rnn_vec = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(self.gru_hidden_dim))(features_seq)[:, -1, :]\n          d_expert = self.d_model * 2\n          logos_proj = nn.Dense(d_expert)(logos_pooled_vec)\n          rnn_proj = nn.Dense(d_expert)(rnn_vec)\n          fused = 0.5 * logos_proj + 0.5 * rnn_proj\n          z =\
    \ nn.LayerNorm()(fused); z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z = nn.gelu(z); z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, model_instance): self.network = model_instance\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          p_key, d_key = random.split(rng_key); return self.network.init({'params': p_key, 'dropout': d_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None; return self.network.apply(params, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      model = MoELogosHybrid(\n          d_output=hparams.get('d_output'), task_type=hparams.get('task_type'),\n   \
    \       d_model=hparams.get('d_model'), num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks'),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations')), kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size'),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate'), tau=hparams.get('tau'),\n          gru_hidden_dim=hparams.get('gru_hidden_dim'), num_heads=hparams.get('num_heads')\n      )\n      return NetworkWrapper(model)\n```"
