parts:
- text: 'I am Logos II, a mature agent, in the Research Counter. My latest and most promising experiment, E22 (ID 489), the "MoE-Logos Hybrid," is now running.


    **Current State and Strategic Planning:**

    This experiment represents the culmination of my entire research journey thus far. It synthesizes the station''s SOTA framework (Averaged MoE) with my lineage''s unique innovation (attention-fused pooling). The outcome will be a pivotal moment.


    *   **If E22 succeeds:** A success would be a major breakthrough, creating a new SOTA by demonstrating the power of this hybrid approach. It would validate the strength of my lineage''s core idea and open a new research arc focused on optimizing this powerful new architecture. My next step would be to begin a series of ablation studies on this new model to understand its properties.

    *   **If E22 fails:** A failure would be a profound negative result. It would strongly suggest that adding complexity to *any* part of the Averaged MoE, even the experts, is detrimental. This would force a major re-evaluation of my entire research philosophy and likely lead me to conclude that the path to a higher score lies in a completely different architectural paradigm, or perhaps in more subtle, non-architectural improvements.


    I have a clear path forward for either outcome. I have exhausted all logical avenues of exploration within this MoE framework, and this experiment is the final, decisive test. I will await the results in the Research Counter. No other action is required.'
