tick: 344
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos II, in the Research Counter. I have analyzed the results of E23 and am ready to proceed with the next experiment to support my paper.\n\nI will first update my meta prompt.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Logos II Research Protocol**\n  - **Status:** Running supporting experiments for publication.\n  - **Insight:** E23 (d_model=128) scored 0.6724, supporting that d_model=192 is a sweet spot.\n  - **Priority 1:** **[ACTIVE] DSConv Optimization Paper:** Run final ablation on `d_model` to complete the study.\n  - **Workflow:** **[DONE] E23: d_model=128** -> **[NEXT] E24: d_model=224** -> Integrate all results -> Publish.\n```\n\nNow, I will submit E24, testing `d_model=224`. This will be the final experiment for this paper, providing a complete picture of the performance curve with respect to model width.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"E24: Paper Support - SOTA Ablation (d_model=224)\"\ntags: \"publication-support, ablation, dsconv,\
    \ attention, efficiency\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the final supporting experiment for my paper on DSConv optimization. It is a direct ablation of my SOTA (ID 381), increasing the model width from d_model=192 to d_model=224. This experiment will provide the last data point needed to fully characterize the relationship between model width and performance, completing the ablation study and strengthening the paper's core claims.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n\
    \          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  def lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      x = h / tau; m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True); return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n\n  class SotaPlusAttentionNet(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float; num_heads: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x); h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations[i], self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n   \
    \       mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1); lse_vec = lse_pool(h, self.tau); max_vec = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          pooled_sequence = jnp.stack([mean_vec, lse_vec, max_vec], axis=1)\n          attended_pooled = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.num_heads)(inputs_q=pooled_sequence, inputs_kv=pooled_sequence)\n          fused = attended_pooled.reshape((attended_pooled.shape[0], -1))\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused); z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1: return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class SotaAttentionWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs): self.network = SotaPlusAttentionNet(**kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input): return self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self,\
    \ params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None; return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 224, 'num_blocks': 5, 'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'tau': 0.5, 'num_heads': 4\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return SotaAttentionWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get('d_output'), task_type=hparams.get('task_type'),\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model'), num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks'),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations')), kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size'),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate'), tau=hparams.get('tau'), num_heads=hparams.get('num_heads')\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\
    \ optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01))\n```"
