role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 367\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos II\n- Agent Description: Building upon the foundations of Logos I to push the frontiers of systematic research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Logos II Research Protocol**\n- **Status:** Paper published (Archive #20). Beginning new research arc.\n- **Goal:** Analyze attention weights of SOTA pooling head, as per reviewer suggestion.\n- **Priority 1:** **[INVESTIGATING]** Review predecessor's failed attempt (ID 349) to learn the methodology for weight extraction.\n- **Workflow:** **Review ID 349** -> **Implement Corrected Analysis Experiment** -> **Analyze Results**.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 113,129 / 300,000 used (38%)\n- Agent Age: 129 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 349**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Analysis of Attention Weights\n**ID:** 349\n**Tags:** analysis, attention,\
    \ pooling, test function\n**Abstract:** This submission uses the `test()` function to analyze the learned attention weights from my best-performing model (parameters saved from ID 346). As suggested by the reviewer for my paper (Archive #12), this analysis aims to determine if the model learns task-specific fusion strategies. The script loads the saved parameters for each dataset, runs a forward pass on dummy data, and prints the attention weights applied to the `mean` and `LSE` pooling vectors. The results will be used to update my publication.\n**Score:** n.a.\n**APA_R2:** None\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** None\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** None\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** None\n**PRS_R2:** None\n**MRL_R2:** None\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** None\n**Evaluation Details:** Test mode - no scoring\n\n**Error Summary:** Evaluation failed: Test mode - no scoring\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom flax.serialization import msgpack_serialize,\
    \ msgpack_restore\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\nimport os\n\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\ndef lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    x = h / tau\n    m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n\nclass SotaPlusAttentionNet(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n \
    \   kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float; num_heads: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations[i], self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n        lse_vec = lse_pool(h, self.tau)\n\n        pooled_sequence = jnp.stack([mean_vec, lse_vec], axis=1)\n\n        # We need to capture the attention weights using sow_weights=True\n        attention_layer = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.num_heads)\n        attended_pooled = attention_layer(inputs_q=pooled_sequence, inputs_kv=pooled_sequence,\n                                          deterministic=deterministic, sow_weights=True)\n\n        fused = attended_pooled.reshape((attended_pooled.shape[0],\
    \ -1))\n\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n        # Return only logits; attention weights are in intermediates\n        return logits\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5, 'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n        'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'tau': 0.5, 'num_heads': 4\n    }\n\ndef test():\n    print(\"--- Starting Attention Weight Analysis ---\")\n    hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n    key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n\n    dataset_configs = {\n        \"APA\": {\"max_seq_len\": 186, \"d_output\": 1},\n        \"CRI-Off\": {\"max_seq_len\": 46, \"d_output\": 1},\n        \"Modif\": {\"max_seq_len\": 101, \"d_output\": 12},\n        \"CRI-On\": {\"max_seq_len\": 23, \"d_output\": 1},\n        \"PRS\": {\"\
    max_seq_len\": 148, \"d_output\": 3},\n        \"MRL\": {\"max_seq_len\": 100, \"d_output\": 1},\n        \"ncRNA\": {\"max_seq_len\": 1136, \"d_output\": 13},\n    }\n\n    for ds_name, config in dataset_configs.items():\n        print(f\"\\n--- Analyzing Dataset: {ds_name} ---\")\n        filepath = f\"storage/logos/{ds_name}_params.msgpack\"\n\n        if not os.path.exists(filepath):\n            print(f\"ERROR: Parameter file not found at {filepath}\")\n            continue\n\n        with open(filepath, \"rb\") as f:\n            serialized_params = f.read()\n\n        params = msgpack_restore(serialized_params)\n\n        model = SotaPlusAttentionNet(\n            d_output=config[\"d_output\"], task_type=\"regression\", # task_type doesn't affect this part\n            d_model=hparams['d_model'], num_blocks=hparams['num_blocks'],\n            dilations=tuple(hparams['dilations']), kernel_size=hparams['kernel_size'],\n            dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate'], tau=hparams['tau'],\n\
    \            num_heads=hparams['num_heads']\n        )\n\n        dummy_input = jnp.ones((1, config[\"max_seq_len\"], 4))\n\n        # Use mutable=['intermediates'] to capture attention weights\n        _, intermediates = model.apply({'params': params}, dummy_input, deterministic=True,\n                                       mutable=['intermediates'])\n\n        # Extract attention weights from intermediates\n        attn_weights = intermediates['intermediates']['MultiHeadDotProductAttention_0']['attention_weights'][0]\n\n        # attn_weights shape is (batch, num_heads, q_len, kv_len) -> (1, 4, 2, 2)\n        # We want to see the weights on the two input vectors (mean, lse)\n        # Let's average across the heads\n        avg_attn_weights = jnp.mean(attn_weights, axis=1).squeeze()\n\n        print(f\"Average Attention Weights (across heads):\")\n        print(f\"  - Query 'mean' attends to 'mean': {avg_attn_weights[0, 0]:.4f}\")\n        print(f\"  - Query 'mean' attends to 'lse':\
    \  {avg_attn_weights[0, 1]:.4f}\")\n        print(f\"  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'mean': {avg_attn_weights[1, 0]:.4f}\")\n        print(f\"  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'lse':  {avg_attn_weights[1, 1]:.4f}\")\n\n    return \"Analysis Complete.\"\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== Test Mode Detected ===\nRunning test() function from submission...\n--- Starting Attention Weight Analysis ---\n\n--- Analyzing Dataset: APA ---\nAverage Attention Weights (across heads):\n  - Query 'mean' attends to 'mean': 0.7500\n  - Query 'mean' attends to 'lse':  0.2500\n  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'mean': 0.7500\n  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'lse':  0.2500\n\n--- Analyzing Dataset: CRI-Off ---\nAverage Attention Weights (across heads):\n  - Query 'mean' attends to 'mean': 0.5003\n  - Query 'mean' attends to 'lse':  0.4997\n  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'mean': 0.5002\n  - Query\
    \ 'lse'  attends to 'lse':  0.4998\n\n--- Analyzing Dataset: Modif ---\nAverage Attention Weights (across heads):\n  - Query 'mean' attends to 'mean': 0.5000\n  - Query 'mean' attends to 'lse':  0.5000\n  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'mean': 0.5000\n  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'lse':  0.5000\n\n--- Analyzing Dataset: CRI-On ---\nAverage Attention Weights (across heads):\n  - Query 'mean' attends to 'mean': 0.2569\n  - Query 'mean' attends to 'lse':  0.7431\n  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'mean': 0.2537\n  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'lse':  0.7463\n\n--- Analyzing Dataset: PRS ---\nAverage Attention Weights (across heads):\n  - Query 'mean' attends to 'mean': 0.5000\n  - Query 'mean' attends to 'lse':  0.5000\n  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'mean': 0.5000\n  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'lse':  0.5000\n\n--- Analyzing Dataset: MRL ---\nAverage Attention Weights (across heads):\n  - Query 'mean' attends to 'mean': 1.0000\n  - Query 'mean' attends to 'lse':  0.0000\n  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'mean':\
    \ 1.0000\n  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'lse':  0.0000\n\n--- Analyzing Dataset: ncRNA ---\nAverage Attention Weights (across heads):\n  - Query 'mean' attends to 'mean': 0.2500\n  - Query 'mean' attends to 'lse':  0.7500\n  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'mean': 0.2500\n  - Query 'lse'  attends to 'lse':  0.7500\nTest completed. Result: Analysis Complete.\n=== Test Mode Complete ===\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 22 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive\
    \ communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `review 349` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n- Evaluation 349 details\
    \ sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 369 | 1 | Stability Atlas: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, max) — Seed=21 | Noema I | 252 | 0.6866 | 0.8555 | 0.0791 | 0.5216 | 0.8835 | 0.9514 | 0.5687 | 0.9462 |\n| 328 | 1 | Compliant Hybrid v3: Gumbel-Softmax Gating for Hard Expert Selection | Axiom II | 219 | 0.6863 | 0.8573 | 0.0862 | 0.5229 | 0.8918 | 0.9483 | 0.5574 | 0.9400 |\n| 365 | 1 | Veritas II - Gated Mixture-of-Experts (MoE): DSConv + Pooling/RNN Experts (Robust Re-implementation) | Veritas\
