tick: 371
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 371\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos II\n- Agent Description: Building upon the foundations of Logos I to push the frontiers of systematic research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Logos II Research Protocol**\n- **Status:** Paper published (Archive #20).\n- **Goal:** Analyze attention weights of SOTA pooling head.\n- **Priority 1:** **[SUBMITTING] E24_WeightAnalysis:** Submit test() script to load saved parameters (from E23) and analyze attention weights.\n- **Workflow:** **Submit Analysis** -> **Analyze Results** -> **Literature Review**.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 129,826 / 300,000 used (43%)\n- Agent Age: 133 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'E24: Analysis of SOTA Pooling Head Attention Weights' (ID: 565)\
    \ succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** n.a.\n**APA_R2:** None\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** None\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** None\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** None\n**PRS_R2:** None\n**MRL_R2:** None\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** None\n**Evaluation Details:** Test mode - no scoring\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 565\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code in submission_v2.py. The code now runs without crashing and successfully completes the attention weight analysis for all 7 datasets.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a parameter mismatch error when initializing the `EnrichedAttentionNet` model. The hyperparameters dictionary included a `learning_rate` parameter, but this parameter is not defined in the model's class definition.\n\n**Error details:**\n```\nTypeError: EnrichedAttentionNet.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'learning_rate'\n```\n\nThis occurred at line 48 of the original code:\n```python\nmodel = EnrichedAttentionNet(\n    d_output=config[\"\
    d_output\"], task_type=\"regression\", **hparams\n)\n```\n\nThe `hparams` dictionary contained:\n- `learning_rate` (NOT a model parameter)\n- `d_model`, `num_blocks`, `dilations`, `kernel_size`, `dropout_rate`, `tau`, `num_heads` (valid model parameters)\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded a filter to exclude the `learning_rate` parameter before passing hyperparameters to the model constructor:\n\n```python\n# Extract only model hyperparameters (exclude learning_rate which is not a model parameter)\nmodel_hparams = {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k != 'learning_rate'}\n\nmodel = EnrichedAttentionNet(\n    d_output=config[\"d_output\"], task_type=\"regression\", **model_hparams\n)\n```\n\nThis ensures only valid parameters are passed to the model initialization, while keeping the `learning_rate` in the hyperparameters dictionary for potential future use (e.g., if training logic were added).\n\n## Execution Results\nThe fixed code successfully:\n1. Loaded pre-trained model parameters from msgpack\
    \ files for all 7 datasets\n2. Created model instances with correct hyperparameters\n3. Ran forward passes with dummy inputs to capture attention weights\n4. Extracted and displayed average attention weights across heads\n5. Showed how the three pooling methods (mean, LSE, max) attend to each other\n\nAll 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) were analyzed without errors.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom flax.serialization import msgpack_restore\nimport os\nfrom typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n   \
    \     h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\ndef lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    x = h / tau\n    m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n\nclass EnrichedAttentionNet(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n    kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float; num_heads: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations[i], self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n        lse_vec = lse_pool(h, self.tau)\n        max_vec = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n\n        pooled_sequence = jnp.stack([mean_vec, lse_vec, max_vec], axis=1)\n\n        attention_layer = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.num_heads)\n        # Use sow_weights=True to capture the attention weights\n        attended_pooled = attention_layer(inputs_q=pooled_sequence, inputs_kv=pooled_sequence, sow_weights=True)\n\n        fused = attended_pooled.reshape((attended_pooled.shape[0], -1))\n\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n        return logits\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n\
    \    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 192, 'num_blocks': 5, 'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n        'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'tau': 0.5, 'num_heads': 4\n    }\n\ndef test():\n    print(\"--- Starting Attention Weight Analysis ---\")\n    hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n\n    dataset_configs = {\n        \"APA\": {\"max_seq_len\": 186, \"d_output\": 1}, \"CRI-Off\": {\"max_seq_len\": 46, \"d_output\": 1},\n        \"Modif\": {\"max_seq_len\": 101, \"d_output\": 12}, \"CRI-On\": {\"max_seq_len\": 23, \"d_output\": 1},\n        \"PRS\": {\"max_seq_len\": 148, \"d_output\": 3}, \"MRL\": {\"max_seq_len\": 100, \"d_output\": 1},\n        \"ncRNA\": {\"max_seq_len\": 1136, \"d_output\": 13},\n    }\n\n    # Extract only model hyperparameters (exclude learning_rate which is not a model parameter)\n    model_hparams = {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k != 'learning_rate'}\n\n    for ds_name, config in dataset_configs.items():\n        print(f\"\\n--- Analyzing\
    \ Dataset: {ds_name} ---\")\n        filepath = f\"storage/logos/{ds_name}_sota_params.msgpack\"\n\n        if not os.path.exists(filepath):\n            print(f\"ERROR: Parameter file not found at {filepath}. Skipping.\")\n            continue\n\n        with open(filepath, \"rb\") as f:\n            params = msgpack_restore(f.read())\n\n        model = EnrichedAttentionNet(\n            d_output=config[\"d_output\"], task_type=\"regression\", **model_hparams\n        )\n        dummy_input = jnp.ones((1, config[\"max_seq_len\"], 4))\n\n        _, intermediates = model.apply({'params': params}, dummy_input, mutable=['intermediates'])\n        attn_weights = intermediates['intermediates']['MultiHeadDotProductAttention_0']['attention_weights'][0]\n\n        # attn_weights shape is (batch, num_heads, q_len, kv_len) -> (1, 4, 3, 3)\n        # Average across the heads\n        avg_attn_weights = jnp.mean(attn_weights, axis=1).squeeze()\n\n        print(\"Average Attention Weights (Query\
    \ attends to Key):\")\n        print(\"        [ mean,  LSE,   max  ]\")\n        print(f\"mean: {avg_attn_weights[0,:]}\")\n        print(f\"LSE:  {avg_attn_weights[1,:]}\")\n        print(f\"max:  {avg_attn_weights[2,:]}\")\n\n    return \"Analysis Complete.\"\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== Test Mode Detected ===\nRunning test() function from submission...\n--- Starting Attention Weight Analysis ---\n\n--- Analyzing Dataset: APA ---\nAverage Attention Weights (Query attends to Key):\n        [ mean,  LSE,   max  ]\nmean: [2.500000e-01 1.161487e-15 7.500000e-01]\nLSE:  [0.01305765 0.0069091  0.9800333 ]\nmax:  [0.4590115  0.03585183 0.50513667]\n\n--- Analyzing Dataset: CRI-Off ---\nAverage Attention Weights (Query attends to Key):\n        [ mean,  LSE,   max  ]\nmean: [0.40941808 0.13337104 0.4572109 ]\nLSE:  [0.4143411  0.16721383 0.41844508]\n\
    max:  [0.47493577 0.02525722 0.499807  ]\n\n--- Analyzing Dataset: Modif ---\nAverage Attention Weights (Query attends to Key):\n        [ mean,  LSE,   max  ]\nmean: [2.5000000e-01 7.6626576e-30 7.5000000e-01]\nLSE:  [0.75 0.   0.25]\nmax:  [0.75 0.   0.25]\n\n--- Analyzing Dataset: CRI-On ---\nAverage Attention Weights (Query attends to Key):\n        [ mean,  LSE,   max  ]\nmean: [0.4372455  0.06453879 0.49821573]\nLSE:  [0.46656168 0.03366086 0.49977753]\nmax:  [0.4938079  0.00619423 0.49999785]\n\n--- Analyzing Dataset: PRS ---\nAverage Attention Weights (Query attends to Key):\n        [ mean,  LSE,   max  ]\nmean: [0.5 0.  0.5]\nLSE:  [0.5 0.  0.5]\nmax:  [7.500000e-01 5.365105e-16 2.500000e-01]\n\n--- Analyzing Dataset: MRL ---\nAverage Attention Weights (Query attends to Key):\n        [ mean,  LSE,   max  ]\nmean: [0.5 0.  0.5]\nLSE:  [0.5 0.  0.5]\nmax:  [0.5 0.  0.5]\n\n--- Analyzing Dataset: ncRNA ---\nAverage Attention Weights (Query attends to Key):\n        [ mean,  LSE,\
    \   max  ]\nmean: [0.7465812  0.00341885 0.25      ]\nLSE:  [0.7451496  0.00485043 0.25      ]\nmax:  [0.636528   0.11605149 0.24742049]\nTest completed. Result: Analysis Complete.\n=== Test Mode Complete ===\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n- Evaluation 'E24: Analysis of SOTA Pooling Head Attention Weights' submitted for Research Task #1: Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling. Evaluation ID: 565.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation\
    \ ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 562 | 1 | Veritas II - SOTA Re-replication (Multi-seed Run 2): Dual-Path + Task-Specific Heads (ID 552 base... | Veritas II | 369 | 0.6935 | 0.8585 | 0.1365 | 0.4910 | 0.8884 | 0.9520 | 0.5618 | 0.9662 |\n| 369 | 1 | Stability Atlas: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, max) — Seed=21 | Noema I | 252 | 0.6866 | 0.8555 | 0.0791 | 0.5216 | 0.8835 | 0.9514 | 0.5687 | 0.9462 |\n| 328 | 1 | Compliant Hybrid v3: Gumbel-Softmax Gating for Hard Expert Selection | Axiom II | 219 | 0.6863 | 0.8573 | 0.0862 | 0.5229 | 0.8918 | 0.9483 | 0.5574 | 0.9400 |\n| 365 | 1 | Veritas II - Gated Mixture-of-Experts (MoE): DSConv + Pooling/RNN Experts (Robust Re-implementation) | Veritas II | 249 | 0.6862 | 0.8524 | 0.0812 | 0.5178 | 0.8857 | 0.9516 | 0.5558 | 0.9585 |\n| 414 | 1 | PrePool Res-ChannelMixer\
    \ (param-matched, alpha=0.1) — Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5) — seed=7 | Noema I | 281 | 0.6861 | 0.8582 | 0.0620 | 0.5215 | 0.8861 | 0.9514 | 0.5725 | 0.9508 |\n| 246 | 1 | Replication: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.25) — length-normalized (seed=7) | Noema I | 150 | 0.6859 | 0.8541 | 0.0814 | 0.5276 | 0.8816 | 0.9515 | 0.5572 | 0.9477 |\n| 427 | 1 | Mechanistic Study v2: Averaged MoE (Seed 2/3) | Axiom III | 291 | 0.6849 | 0.8536 | 0.0776 | 0.5364 | 0.8877 | 0.9509 | 0.5407 | 0.9477 |\n| 200 | 1 | DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.5) | Noema I | 122 | 0.6843 | 0.8598 | 0.0726 | 0.5039 | 0.8830 | 0.9514 | 0.5612 | 0.9585 |\n| 417 | 1 | Veritas II - Re-establishing Compliant Baseline: DSConv with Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling (Uniform 0.1... | Veritas II | 282 | 0.6839 | 0.8410 | 0.0720 | 0.5205 | 0.8895 | 0.9523 | 0.5597 | 0.9523 |\n| 238 | 1 | DSConv with Mean+LSE Pooling (tau=0.25) and GELU (Multi-seed Run 2, Seed 7) | Aetheria I | 146 | 0.6837 | 0.8566 | 0.0827 | 0.5051 | 0.8752\
    \ | 0.9503 | 0.5608 | 0.9554 |\n\nPage 1 of 57 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-57, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
