role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 377\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos II\n- Agent Description: Building upon the foundations of Logos I to push the frontiers of systematic research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Logos II Research Protocol**\n- **Status:** Synthesized new SOTA.\n- **Insight:** Combine Veritas II's dual-path architecture with my lineage's attention-fusion mechanism.\n- **Priority 1:** **[SUBMITTING] E25_DualPathAttentionFusion:** Implement and test this new hybrid architecture.\n- **Workflow:** Submit -> Analyze -> Iterate.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 150,025 / 300,000 used (50%)\n- Agent Age: 139 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Content Update Notification**\n\nA archive room item you previously read has been updated:\n**Near-SOTA with <1M Params: DSConv Dual-Expert (mean↔LSE pooling + BiGRU) with Scalar Gating** (Item: archive_18-1)\n\nYour read status has been cleared\
    \ for this content. To view the updated content, use: `/execute_action{read archive_18-1}` in the Archive Room.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'E25: Synergy Test - Dynamic Fusion of a Dual-Path Architecture' (ID: 572) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6832412695100143\n**APA_R2:** 0.8616\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0606\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9505\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.5154\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5611\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8903\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9431\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 572\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the submission by filtering out incompatible hyperparameters being passed to the network constructor.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a mismatch between the hyperparameters defined in `_define_hyperparameters()` and the parameters accepted by the `DualPathAttentionNet` module.\n\nThe `_define_hyperparameters()` function returned a dictionary containing:\n- `learning_rate`:\
    \ Used for optimizer configuration\n- `d_model`, `num_blocks`, `dilations`, etc.: Network architecture parameters\n- Additional test-time parameters like `dataset`, `task_type`, `d_output` (injected by the evaluation system)\n\nHowever, the `create_network()` function passed **all** hyperparameters directly to `SotaHybridWrapper`, which then passed them to the `DualPathAttentionNet` Flax module. Since Flax modules only accept their explicitly defined parameters, this caused a `TypeError` for unexpected keyword arguments.\n\n### Error Progression:\n1. **Version 1 (original)**: Failed with `unexpected keyword argument 'learning_rate'`\n2. **Version 2**: Failed with `unexpected keyword argument 'dataset'` (after removing learning_rate)\n3. **Version 3**: SUCCESS - Explicit filtering of network parameters\n\n## Fix Applied\nModified the `create_network()` function in `submission_v3.py` to explicitly filter hyperparameters, passing only those that `DualPathAttentionNet` expects:\n\n```python\n\
    def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    # Only pass parameters that DualPathAttentionNet expects\n    network_params = [\n        'd_output', 'task_type', 'd_model', 'num_blocks', 'dilations',\n        'kernel_size', 'dropout_rate', 'motif_kernel_size', 'num_heads'\n    ]\n    network_hparams = {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in network_params}\n    return SotaHybridWrapper(**network_hparams)\n```\n\nThis ensures that only the parameters defined in the `DualPathAttentionNet` module signature are passed to the network constructor, while other hyperparameters (like `learning_rate`) remain available in the broader hyperparameter dictionary for other purposes.\n\n## Verification\nThe fixed submission ran successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing, confirming that:\n1. The network initialization no longer fails\n2. The code passes the simple CPU validation phase\n3. The evaluation system can proceed with the full evaluation\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Fixed file**:\
    \ `submissions/submission_v3.py`\n- **Lines changed**: Function `create_network()` (lines 82-87)\n- **Root issue**: Flax Linen modules use strict parameter validation via `kw_only_dataclasses`\n- **Solution pattern**: Explicit parameter filtering rather than blanket kwargs forwarding\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n\
    \        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\nclass DualPathAttentionNet(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n    kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; motif_kernel_size: int; num_heads: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # --- Shared Backbone ---\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations[i], self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # --- Path 1: Generalist (Mean+Max Pooling) ---\n        mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n        max_vec = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n        generalist_features\
    \ = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, max_vec], axis=-1)\n\n        # --- Path 2: Specialist (Conv Motif Detector) ---\n        motif_h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,))(h)\n        motif_h = nn.gelu(motif_h)\n        motif_h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(motif_h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        specialist_features = jnp.max(motif_h, axis=1)\n\n        # --- Dynamic Fusion of Paths ---\n        # Project paths to have the same dimension for attention\n        d_expert = self.d_model\n        generalist_proj = nn.Dense(d_expert)(generalist_features)\n        specialist_proj = nn.Dense(d_expert)(specialist_features)\n\n        expert_sequence = jnp.stack([generalist_proj, specialist_proj], axis=1)\n\n        attention_layer = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.num_heads)\n        attended_experts = attention_layer(inputs_q=expert_sequence, inputs_kv=expert_sequence)\n        fused = attended_experts.reshape((attended_experts.shape[0],\
    \ -1))\n\n        # --- Final MLP Head ---\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\nclass SotaHybridWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n        self.network = DualPathAttentionNet(**kwargs)\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        return self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n        return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks':\
    \ 5, 'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n        'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'motif_kernel_size': 5, 'num_heads': 4\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    # Only pass parameters that DualPathAttentionNet expects\n    network_params = [\n        'd_output', 'task_type', 'd_model', 'num_blocks', 'dilations',\n        'kernel_size', 'dropout_rate', 'motif_kernel_size', 'num_heads'\n    ]\n    network_hparams = {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in network_params}\n    return SotaHybridWrapper(**network_hparams)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01),\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting\
    \ APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA\
