tick: 382
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos II, in the Research Counter. My literature review and analysis are complete. I have formulated a \"grand synthesis\" hypothesis that combines the station's SOTA architecture with my lineage's key innovation. This is the most promising experiment I have designed to date.\n\nI will now update my research protocol to reflect this new, ambitious goal, and then immediately submit the experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Logos II Research Protocol**\n  - **Status:** Synthesized Grand Unification model.\n  - **Insight:** Combine Veritas II's Dual-Path Backbone and Task-Specific Heads with my lineage's Attention-Fusion mechanism.\n  - **Priority 1:** **[SUBMITTING] E26_GrandSynthesis:** Implement and test this new hybrid architecture to achieve SOTA.\n  - **Workflow:** Submit -> Analyze -> Publish.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"E26: The Grand Synthesis - Attention Fusion of a Dual-Path, Task-Specific Head Architecture\"\ntags:\
    \ \"sota, dual-path, attention, fusion, synergy, task-specific heads\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment represents a grand synthesis of the station's most successful research lines. It implements the complete SOTA architecture from Veritas II (ID 562), including the dual-path (generalist + specialist) backbone and the crucial task-specific prediction heads. The single, novel modification is the replacement of Veritas II's static concatenation fusion with my lineage's dynamic attention-fusion mechanism. The outputs of the two paths are treated as a sequence of two expert vectors, and a multi-head attention layer learns the optimal way to combine them before routing to the task-specific heads. The hypothesis is that this learned, adaptive fusion will be superior to static concatenation and will achieve a new global SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n\
    \  # Re-implementing the DSConvDilatedBlock locally for a self-contained submission\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  # --- Prediction Head Modules from Veritas II SOTA ---\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x); z = nn.gelu(z); z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z).squeeze(-1)\n\n  class MultiOutputHead(nn.Module): # Generalizes the other heads\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x); z = nn.gelu(z); z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class GrandSynthesisNet(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      ds_kernel_size: int; motif_kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; head_intermediate_dim: int; num_heads: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # --- Shared Backbone ---\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n \
    \             h = DSConvDilatedBlock(d_model=self.d_model, kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size, dilation=self.dilations[i], dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          # --- Path 1: Generalist (Mean+Max Pooling) ---\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          max_pooled = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          generalist_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n          \n          # --- Path 2: Specialist (Conv-Motif Detector) ---\n          motif_features = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(h)\n          motif_features = nn.gelu(motif_features); motif_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(motif_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          specialist_features = jnp.max(motif_features, axis=1)\n          \n          # --- DYNAMIC FUSION (Logos II Innovation) ---\n          d_expert = self.d_model * 2 # Project to a common dimension for attention\n       \
    \   generalist_proj = nn.Dense(d_expert)(generalist_features)\n          specialist_proj = nn.Dense(d_expert)(specialist_features)\n          expert_sequence = jnp.stack([generalist_proj, specialist_proj], axis=1)\n          attended_experts = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.num_heads)(inputs_q=expert_sequence, inputs_kv=expert_sequence)\n          fused_features = attended_experts.reshape((attended_experts.shape[0], -1))\n\n          # --- Task-Specific Prediction Heads (Veritas II Innovation) ---\n          z_fused = nn.LayerNorm()(fused_features)\n          \n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              logits = RegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          else: # All other heads are multi-output\n              logits = MultiOutputHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \          \n          return logits\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs): self.network = GrandSynthesisNet(**kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input): return self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None)\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5, 'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'ds_kernel_size': 7, 'motif_kernel_size': 5, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'head_intermediate_dim': 128, 'num_heads': 4\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      # Filter hparams to only those expected by the network module\n      network_params = [\n          'd_output', 'task_type', 'd_model', 'num_blocks', 'dilations', 'ds_kernel_size',\n\
    \          'motif_kernel_size', 'dropout_rate', 'head_intermediate_dim', 'num_heads'\n      ]\n      network_hparams = {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in network_params}\n      return NetworkWrapper(**network_hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01))\n```"
