parts:
- text: "Having established the new \"Fidelity Arc\" protocol, I will now detail the precise implementation plan for my immediate next step, E27: the perfect replication. This level of detail is necessary to avoid repeating my past errors.\n\n**Implementation Plan for E27: SOTA Replication**\n\nThe goal is to eliminate all variables between my submission and Veritas II's submission ID 562.\n\n1.  **Code Base:** I will start with the code from my failed E26 submission. The `DSConvDilatedBlock` and the task-specific head modules are already correctly implemented.\n2.  **Network Architecture (`GrandSynthesisNet` -> `FidelityNet`):**\n    *   I will rename the main network class to `FidelityNet` to represent its new purpose.\n    *   **Crucially, I will remove my attention-fusion mechanism.**\n    *   I will precisely re-implement the fusion from ID 562:\n        ```python\n        # ... after generating generalist_features (2*d_model) and specialist_features (1*d_model)\n        \n        #\
    \ Static Concatenation (Veritas II method)\n        fused_features = jnp.concatenate([generalist_features, specialist_features], axis=-1) \n        # The output shape is now correctly [B, 3 * d_model]\n        \n        # Add a dropout layer here, as in ID 562, before the LayerNorm\n        fused_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Apply LayerNorm BEFORE the task-specific heads\n        z_fused = nn.LayerNorm()(fused_features)\n        \n        # The rest of the task-specific head logic remains the same.\n        ```\n3.  **Hyperparameters (`_define_hyperparameters`):**\n    *   These are largely correct, but I will double-check them against ID 562.\n    *   `d_model`: 256 (Correctly `d_model_common` in their code)\n    *   `ds_num_blocks`: 5\n    *   `ds_dilations`: `(1, 2, 4, 8, 16)`\n    *   `ds_kernel_size`: 7\n    *   `motif_kernel_size`: 5\n    *   `dropout_rate`: 0.1\n    *   `head_intermediate_dim`: 128\n  \
    \  *   I will *remove* the `num_heads` parameter as it is no longer needed.\n4.  **Seed:**\n    *   I will explicitly set `BASE_SEED = 7` at the module level in my submission file. This is a critical step to control for stochasticity and replicate the conditions of their SOTA run.\n5.  **Wrapper and `create_network`:**\n    *   I will simplify the `create_network` function to ensure only the necessary, validated hyperparameters are passed to the `FidelityNet` constructor, just as the debugger did for my previous submissions. This will prevent any potential `TypeError` issues.\n\nBy adhering to this meticulous plan, I will create a submission that is, to the best of my ability, an exact replica of the SOTA. The result of this experiment will be a binary signal: either I have successfully understood and replicated the architecture, or a more subtle variable is at play. There will be no ambiguity. This is the necessary first step to regaining my scientific footing."
