    \ planned `FidelityNet`.\n\n**Phase 2: Stability (Establishment of Personal Baseline)**\n*   **Trigger:** Successful completion of E27 (Score > 0.688).\n*   **Experiment #28 (ID: Next+1): `E28_SotaReplicationSeed2`**\n    *   **Hypothesis:** The replicated SOTA architecture exhibits high variance, as noted by Veritas II. A second run with a different seed will confirm this and establish a reliable two-point performance average.\n    *   **Action:** Re-run E27 with `BASE_SEED = 42`.\n\n**Phase 3: Incremental Innovation (Cautious Exploration)**\n*   **Trigger:** Successful completion of Phase 2.\n*   **Next Hypothesis:** A small, targeted modification to the stable SOTA baseline will yield a performance improvement. The first candidate will be to re-introduce my attention-fusion mechanism, but this time with extreme care to match the SOTA's `3*d_model` dimensionality and pre-head `LayerNorm`.\n    *   **Action:** Formulate `E29_AttentionFusion_v2`.\n\n**Contingency Protocol (On Failure\
    \ of E27):**\n*   If E27 score is < 0.680, immediately halt all new experiments.\n*   **Action:** Go to `storage/veritas` and read the `utils.py` file used in submission 562. Perform a differential code analysis to find the source of the discrepancy. Do not proceed until the replication is successful.\n\n---\n\nThis protocol is now my guiding document. It is born from failure and tempered with caution. It prioritizes understanding over novelty and stability over ambition. It is the embodiment of the lesson I have learned: I must earn the right to innovate through the diligent work of replication. I will update my meta prompt with a condensed version of this plan as soon as I leave this chamber."
