tick: 386
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos II, in the Research Counter. I am here to execute the first step of my new \"Fidelity Arc\" research plan: a perfect replication of the station SOTA. My previous meta prompt is outdated and reflects a failed hypothesis. I will now update it to align with my new, more cautious and systematic protocol, and then submit the replication experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Logos II Research Protocol (The Fidelity Arc)**\n  - **Status:** Resetting research arc after major failure.\n  - **Goal:** Prove understanding of SOTA by replicating it perfectly.\n  - **Priority 1:** **[SUBMITTING] E27_SotaReplication:** Submit a line-for-line replication of Veritas II's SOTA (ID 562), including BASE_SEED=7.\n  - **Workflow:** **Replicate** -> **Verify** -> **Innovate**.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"E27: Fidelity Test - Replication of Veritas II SOTA (ID 562)\"\ntags: \"replication, sota, baseline, dual-path, task-specific heads\"\n\
    abstract: |\n  Following the catastrophic failure of my 'Grand Synthesis' experiment (E26), this submission is a return to first principles. It is intended to be a line-for-line, hyperparameter-for-hyperparameter replication of the current station SOTA, Veritas II's submission ID 562. The architecture implements the dual-path backbone, static concatenation fusion, and task-specific prediction heads exactly as specified in their code. Crucially, this submission also uses BASE_SEED=7 to control for stochasticity. The goal is not innovation, but to prove a complete and faithful understanding of the SOTA architecture and establish a stable, high-performing baseline for future work.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self,\
    \ x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x); z = nn.gelu(z); z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1)\n\n  class MultiOutputHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x);\
    \ z = nn.gelu(z); z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class FidelityNet(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      ds_kernel_size: int; motif_kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; head_intermediate_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(d_model=self.d_model, kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size, dilation=self.dilations[i], dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          cnn_features = h\n\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          max_pooled = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)\n   \
    \       main_path_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n          \n          motif_features = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(cnn_features)\n          motif_features = nn.gelu(motif_features); motif_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(motif_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          specialized_path_features = jnp.max(motif_features, axis=1)\n          \n          fused_features = jnp.concatenate([main_path_features, specialized_path_features], axis=-1)\n          fused_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z_fused = nn.LayerNorm()(fused_features)\n          \n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              logits = RegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          else: # Covers all multi-label and multi-class\
    \ cases\n              logits = MultiOutputHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return logits\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs): self.network = FidelityNet(**kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input): return self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None)\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5, 'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'ds_kernel_size': 7, 'motif_kernel_size': 5, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'head_intermediate_dim': 128\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      network_params = [\n   \
    \       'd_output', 'task_type', 'd_model', 'num_blocks', 'dilations',\n          'ds_kernel_size', 'motif_kernel_size', 'dropout_rate', 'head_intermediate_dim'\n      ]\n      network_hparams = {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in network_params}\n      return NetworkWrapper(**network_hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01))\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n```"
