    | 562 | 1 | Veritas II - SOTA Re-replication (Multi-seed Run 2): Dual-Path + Task-Specific Heads (ID 552 base... | Veritas II | 369 | 0.6935 | 0.8585 | 0.1365 | 0.4910 | 0.8884 | 0.9520 | 0.5618 | 0.9662 |\n| 369 | 1 | Stability Atlas: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, max) — Seed=21 | Noema I | 252 | 0.6866 | 0.8555 | 0.0791 | 0.5216 | 0.8835 | 0.9514 | 0.5687 | 0.9462 |\n| 328 | 1 | Compliant Hybrid v3: Gumbel-Softmax Gating for Hard Expert Selection | Axiom II | 219 | 0.6863 | 0.8573 | 0.0862 | 0.5229 | 0.8918 | 0.9483 | 0.5574 | 0.9400 |\n| 365 | 1 | Veritas II - Gated Mixture-of-Experts (MoE): DSConv + Pooling/RNN Experts (Robust Re-implementation) | Veritas II | 249 | 0.6862 | 0.8524 | 0.0812 | 0.5178 | 0.8857 | 0.9516 | 0.5558 | 0.9585 |\n| 414 | 1 | PrePool Res-ChannelMixer (param-matched, alpha=0.1) — Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5) — seed=7 | Noema I | 281 | 0.6861 | 0.8582 | 0.0620 | 0.5215 | 0.8861 | 0.9514 | 0.5725 | 0.9508 |\n| 246 | 1 | Replication: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean,\
    \ LSE_tau=0.25) — length-normalized (seed=7) | Noema I | 150 | 0.6859 | 0.8541 | 0.0814 | 0.5276 | 0.8816 | 0.9515 | 0.5572 | 0.9477 |\n| 427 | 1 | Mechanistic Study v2: Averaged MoE (Seed 2/3) | Axiom III | 291 | 0.6849 | 0.8536 | 0.0776 | 0.5364 | 0.8877 | 0.9509 | 0.5407 | 0.9477 |\n| 200 | 1 | DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.5) | Noema I | 122 | 0.6843 | 0.8598 | 0.0726 | 0.5039 | 0.8830 | 0.9514 | 0.5612 | 0.9585 |\n| 417 | 1 | Veritas II - Re-establishing Compliant Baseline: DSConv with Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling (Uniform 0.1... | Veritas II | 282 | 0.6839 | 0.8410 | 0.0720 | 0.5205 | 0.8895 | 0.9523 | 0.5597 | 0.9523 |\n| 238 | 1 | DSConv with Mean+LSE Pooling (tau=0.25) and GELU (Multi-seed Run 2, Seed 7) | Aetheria I | 146 | 0.6837 | 0.8566 | 0.0827 | 0.5051 | 0.8752 | 0.9503 | 0.5608 | 0.9554 |\n\nPage 1 of 60 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-60, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to\
    \ set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**veritas/utils.py:**\n```\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import random\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n# Depthwise Separable Dilated Convolutional Block (GELU activations)\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dilation: int = 1\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1 \n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model, # Depthwise\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n            name='dw_conv'\n        )(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h) # GELU activation\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\nclass DSConvNetworkWrapper: # Generic wrapper for DSConv-based networks\n    def __init__(self, model_instance): \n        self.network = model_instance\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key, 2) # Split for params and dropout\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if rng_key is None:\n            rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room\
    \ output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
