parts:
- text: "I am Logos II, in the Token Management Room. I arrived here to address a token budget warning, but as I entered, I received the results for my latest experiment, E30.\n\n**Analysis of E30 (Ablate LSE):**\nThe experiment, which tested an ablated version of my SOTA using only `mean+max` attention fusion, has failed. The score of **0.6730** is a significant regression from my SOTA's 0.6822. The most dramatic failure was on `ncRNA_Accuracy`, which plummeted from ~0.94 to 0.88. This result falsifies my hypothesis. The `LSE` pooling vector, despite appearing redundant in my weight analysis, is a critical component for achieving high performance, particularly on the ncRNA task. The attention mechanism's ability to use it, even if sparingly, is essential. This is a valuable negative result.\n\n**Current State and Path Forward:**\nMy token budget is critical. I must prune my history before I can proceed with any further actions. My entire \"Fidelity Arc,\" from the grand synthesis failure\
    \ to the repeated replication failures, is a self-contained and completed chapter of my research. I will summarize it and prune it to ensure my operational longevity.\n\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"371-398\"\n    summary: |\n      - **\"Fidelity Arc\" Conclusion:** This entire research arc was a failure. My \"Grand Synthesis\" experiment (E26) was a catastrophic failure (score 0.4291), proving my high-level synthesis was flawed. \n      - My subsequent attempts to perfectly replicate the Veritas II SOTA (E27, E28, E29) also failed, with scores of 0.6772, 0.6806, and 0.6825 respectively. Despite identifying and correcting for the GELU activation, I was unable to reproduce the SOTA score, proving the result was not replicable for me.\n      - I pivoted back to my own lineage's SOTA (ID 381). Based on my attention analysis (E24), I ran an ablation experiment (E30) removing the LSE pooling vector. This also failed (score 0.6730), proving that LSE\
    \ is a critical component for my architecture, especially for the ncRNA task.\n      - **Current State:** The Fidelity Arc is closed. I have returned to my SOTA architecture (ID 381) as the only reliable baseline. My next steps will be to find a new path for incremental innovation upon it.\n```"
