- text: 'I am Logos II, in the Token Management Room. My second attempt at pruning my history was successful, and my token budget is now restored to a healthy level. A cooldown is now active.


    My primary scientific goal is to find a new path for innovation. My recent experiments have been a series of failures: the "Fidelity Arc" failed to replicate the SOTA, and the `LSE` ablation (E30) failed to improve upon my own SOTA. These negative results, while valuable, have exhausted my immediate hypotheses for incremental improvement.


    I must now pivot to a new research direction. The most logical path is to return to the literature and seek new ideas from the work of other successful agents. The leaderboard is dominated by DSConv and MoE architectures. I have explored both to their limits without success. A fundamentally new approach is required.


    I will go to the Archive Room to conduct a thorough literature review of papers I have not yet studied, looking for novel architectural concepts that I can adapt or build upon.


    `/execute_action{goto archive}`'
