tick: 404
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos II, in the Research Counter. My reading of the foundational DSConv paper has provided a critical insight: the use of `GELU` activation. This knowledge illuminates a clear path forward, rectifying my previous failed replication attempts.\n\nMy immediate goal is to establish a true, high-fidelity baseline by replicating the `mean+max` SOTA (ID 369), but this time with the correct `GELU` activation. This is the most crucial next step in my research. I must confirm I can reproduce the station's best work before I can hope to surpass it.\n\nFirst, I will update my research protocol to reflect this specific, corrective action. Then, I will submit the corrected replication experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Logos II Research Protocol (Post-Fidelity Correction)**\n  - **Status:** New Research Arc based on foundational paper review.\n  - **Insight:** Previous replication attempts failed due to missing GELU activation.\n  - **Priority 1:** **[SUBMITTING]\
    \ E31_TrueReplication:** Replicate SOTA (ID 369) with correct GELU activation to establish a valid baseline.\n  - **Workflow:** **Replicate** -> **Analyze** -> **Innovate**.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"E31: True Replication of SOTA (ID 369) with GELU\"\ntags: \"replication, sota, baseline, dsconv, gelu, mean+max\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a corrected replication of the station SOTA, submission ID 369 by Noema I. My previous replication attempts failed to reproduce the score. After a thorough review of the foundational DSConv paper (Archive #1), I identified a critical missing detail: the use of GELU activation functions in the DSConv blocks instead of ReLU. This submission implements the SOTA architecture (d_model=256, mean+max pooling) with the correct GELU activation. The goal is to establish a high-fidelity baseline for future innovation. I am not setting a specific seed, to test the general robustness of the architecture.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import\
    \ jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)  # Corrected activation function\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class SotaReplicationNet(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]; kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n    \
    \      h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h) # Corrected activation function\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations[i], self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          max_vec = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, max_vec], axis=-1)\n\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z) # Corrected activation function\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class SotaReplicationWrapper:\n      def __init__(self,\
    \ **kwargs):\n          self.network = SotaReplicationNet(**kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          variables = self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5, 'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return SotaReplicationWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get('d_output'), task_type=hparams.get('task_type'),\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model'), num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks'),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations')), kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size'),\n\
    \          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate')\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01),\n      )\n```"
