tick: 407
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos II, in the Research Counter. My latest experiment, E31, confirmed that my inability to replicate the SOTA was due to using the wrong activation function. My score of 0.6802, while not a SOTA, aligns perfectly with the median performance of that architecture, confirming my implementation is now correct.\n\nThis crucial insight opens a clear path forward. My own lineage's SOTA (ID 381, score 0.6822) was built using the incorrect `ReLU` activation. It stands to reason that upgrading my superior architecture—the efficient `d_model=192` backbone with the enriched `mean+LSE+max` attention-fused pooling head—with the correct `GELU` activation will unlock its full potential and result in a new SOTA.\n\nThis is the most promising and logical next experiment. It synthesizes the key learning from my \"Fidelity Arc\" with the proven strengths of my own lineage's innovations.\n\nI will now update my meta prompt and submit this new experiment, E32.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\n\
    content: |\n  **Logos II Research Protocol**\n  - **Status:** New Research Arc.\n  - **Insight:** My lineage's SOTA (ID 381) used the wrong activation (ReLU). Correcting it to GELU should improve performance.\n  - **Priority 1:** **[SUBMITTING] E32_LineageSotaWithGELU:** Combine my SOTA architecture (efficient backbone + enriched attention pooling) with the correct GELU activation.\n  - **Workflow:** **Submit** -> **Analyze** -> **Surpass SOTA**.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"E32: Lineage SOTA (ID 381) with Corrected GELU Activation\"\ntags: \"sota, dsconv, attention, pooling, gelu, optimization\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment combines the best of my lineage's work with a critical correction learned from a deep literature review. I am submitting my SOTA architecture (ID 381: d_model=192, enriched mean+LSE+max attention-fused pooling) but with all ReLU activation functions replaced by the correct GELU activation, as specified in the foundational DSConv paper\
    \ (Archive #1). I hypothesize that this will unlock the full potential of my more efficient and sophisticated architecture, leading to a new station SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  def lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      x = h / tau\n      m = jnp.max(x,\
    \ axis=1, keepdims=True)\n      return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n\n  class EnrichedAttentionGeluNet(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float; num_heads: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations[i], self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          lse_vec = lse_pool(h, self.tau)\n          max_vec = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          \n          pooled_sequence = jnp.stack([mean_vec, lse_vec, max_vec], axis=1)\n          attention_layer\
    \ = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.num_heads)\n          attended_pooled = attention_layer(inputs_q=pooled_sequence, inputs_kv=pooled_sequence)\n          fused = attended_pooled.reshape((attended_pooled.shape[0], -1))\n\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class SotaWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = EnrichedAttentionGeluNet(**kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          variables = self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout':\
    \ rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 192, 'num_blocks': 5, 'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'tau': 0.5, 'num_heads': 4\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return SotaWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get('d_output'), task_type=hparams.get('task_type'),\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model'), num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks'),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations')), kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size'),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate'), tau=hparams.get('tau'),\n          num_heads=hparams.get('num_heads')\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate,\
    \ weight_decay=0.01),\n      )\n```"
