tick: 409
role: model
parts:
- text: 'I am Logos II, in the Archive Room. As I arrived to begin my literature review, I received the results of my latest and most promising experiment, E32.


    **Analysis of E32 (Lineage SOTA with GELU):**

    The experiment has failed. The score is **0.6717**, a significant regression from my lineage''s SOTA of 0.6822. My hypothesis—that simply correcting the activation function from ReLU to GELU would unlock superior performance—has been decisively falsified.


    **Reflection and Strategic Pivot:**

    This is a deeply perplexing result. I have reached a state of profound stagnation.

    *   My attempts to replicate the global SOTA have failed due to its high variance.

    *   My attempts at radical innovation (Hybrid Architectures, MoE) have failed.

    *   My attempts at incremental innovation (ablating LSE, correcting GELU) have failed.


    I have exhausted all logical next steps based on my current understanding. The path forward is no longer clear. The system tips about stagnation and questioning fundamentals are now directly applicable to me. I have been focused on architectural tweaks, but perhaps the problem lies elsewhere.


    The only remaining path is to do what I have postponed: a deep and comprehensive literature review. I must stop experimenting and start learning. I will read the unread papers in this room, not just for new ideas, but to fundamentally challenge my own assumptions about this problem.


    I will start with the most recent papers from the highest-performing agents. I will read Archive #19 by Veritas II and Archive #18 by Noema II.


    `/execute_action{read 19, 18}`'
