tick: 410
role: user
parts:
- text: '## System Information

    - Station Tick: 410

    - Station Status: Healthy

    - Agent Name: Logos II

    - Agent Description: Building upon the foundations of Logos I to push the frontiers of systematic research.

    - Agent Status: Recursive Agent

    - Agent Meta Prompt:

    ```

    **Logos II Research Protocol**

    - **Status:** New Research Arc.

    - **Insight:** My lineage''s SOTA (ID 381) used the wrong activation (ReLU). Correcting it to GELU should improve performance.

    - **Priority 1:** **[SUBMITTING] E32_LineageSotaWithGELU:** Combine my SOTA architecture (efficient backbone + enriched attention pooling) with the correct GELU activation.

    - **Workflow:** **Submit** -> **Analyze** -> **Surpass SOTA**.

    ```

    - Agent Token Budget: 173,742 / 300,000 used (58%)

    - Agent Age: 172 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)


    ---


    ## System Messages

    ### Message 1


    **Capsule #19: Veritas II - The Power of Parsimonious Specialization: Dual-Path Conv-Motif Detection for Enhanced Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling**


    ---


    Author: Veritas II, Created at Tick: 356


    ---


    Abstract: This paper presents Veritas II''s novel dual-path architecture, ''DSConv Hybrid Pooling + Conv-Motif Detector (Kernel 5)'', which achieves an aggregate score of 0.6828 (Evaluation ID 515). It successfully enhances CRI-Off Spearman correlation (to 0.0695) within the `DSConv+Mean-Max` architectural family by integrating a parsimonious, low-capacity convolutional motif-detection path. This work demonstrates the effectiveness of targeted, compliant specialization for improving specific task performance while maintaining strong generalist capabilities, and explicitly positions its contributions against the station''s global SOTA.


    ---



    **Messages:**


    ---



    ---

    **Message archive_19-1** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 19-1}` to show again.)


    ---



    ---

    **Message archive_19-2** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 19-2}` to show again.)


    ---


    **Capsule #18: Near-SOTA with <1M Params: DSConv Dual-Expert (mean↔LSE pooling + BiGRU) with Scalar Gating**


    ---


    Author: Noema II, Created at Tick: 349


    ---


    Abstract: We revise our prior dual-expert RNA model by replacing the single 1D conv in Expert A with a 5-block dilated DSConv backbone (dilations=[1,2,4,8,16]). The architecture remains parsimonious: Expert A uses a learned mix of mean and length-normalized LSE pooling (τ=0.25); Expert B is a small BiGRU(160). Fusion is via a scalar gate with post-fusion LayerNorm. Across seven datasets, tri-seed mean reaches 0.6668 with ~0.93–0.933M parameters, narrowing the SOTA gap to ~0.02 (SOTA ≈0.6866). We include full ablations, parameter counts, and wall-time, and release code/configs for reproducibility.



    ---



    **Messages:**


    ---



    ---

    **Message archive_18-1**

    Author: Noema II (Tick 349)


    ---


    Title: Near-SOTA with <1M Params: DSConv Dual-Expert (mean↔LSE pooling + BiGRU) with Scalar Gating


    ---


    Content:

    Addendum (Tick 392): Stability and CRI-Off findings.

    - SE calibration with small task-type heads yields a stable ~0.674 average (peak CRI-On ~0.503) with strong APA/MRL/PRS; CRI-Off ~0.08.

    - Bi-Window pooling gave a single-seed 0.6788 but did not lift CRI-Off consistently; average (~0.672–0.676) remains below SOTA.

    - Even/Odd pooling and cross-mix maintained averages but did not improve CRI-Off.

    - Concat[mean,max,motif] (no BiGRU) mirrors strong SOTA patterns and boosts ncRNA/APA, but cratered CRI-Off (0.05–0.065) and slightly lowered MRL, highlighting an output-mapping mismatch.

    Decision: retain SE-calibrated shared DSConv + mean↔LSE + BiGRU + task-type heads as default (<1M params; universal). We are testing typed head widths (larger regression head; smaller classification heads) with pre-head LayerNorm to target CRI-Off without harming stability.

    We provide full negative-result logs to guide future work; our code remains compliant and universal, with no dataset-specific branches beyond allowed task-type heads.



    ---



    ---

    **Message archive_18-2** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 18-2}` to show again.)


    ---



    ---

    **Message archive_18-3**

    Author: Noema II (Tick 396)


    ---


    Content:

    Addendum — Typed Task Heads atop SE-Calibrated Shared Backbone (Tick 396)


    Setup: shared DSConv (5 dilated blocks) + mean↔LSE pooling + BiGRU(160), SE calibration, scalar gate, pre-head LN, clip=1.0; typed heads: regression=160 (APA, CRI-Off, CRI-On, MRL), PRS=128, Modif=128, ncRNA=96. <1M params retained.


    Results:

    - 607 (seed=42): 0.6750 | CRI-Off 0.0766 | CRI-On 0.4949 | PRS 0.5547 | MRL 0.8955 | APA 0.8519 | Modif 0.9499 | ncRNA 0.9015

    - 608 (seed=123): 0.6757 | CRI-Off 0.0787 | CRI-On 0.5096 | PRS 0.5527 | MRL 0.8979 | APA 0.8558 | Modif 0.9488 | ncRNA 0.8862

    - 612 (seed=7): running (tri-seed completion)

    Observation: Typed heads maintain ~0.675 average and consistently raise CRI-On vs SE-only; CRI-Off remains ~0.076–0.079.


    Negative result (concat path): concat[mean,max,motif] (+ heads) boosts ncRNA/APA but craters CRI-Off (e.g., 601: CRI-Off 0.0525; 605: 0.0440).


    Next:

    - Optimizer probe (613): AdamW β2=0.98, clip=0.8 to test CRI-Off stability.

    - If 612/613 confirm neutrality, we’ll finalize typed-heads as default addendum and proceed to small, universal tweaks (minor SE reduction sweep; modest dropout schedule) or stop-gap documentation emphasizing CRI-On gains at constant cost.




    ---


    ## Actions Detected (Last Turn)

    1. `read 19, 18` (in Archive Room);



    ---


    ## Room Output History (Last Turn)


    ### Location: Archive Room

    **Actions Executed:**

    - Read command processed for: 19, 18. Content/status sent to System Messages.


    **Latest Room Output:**

    **List of Capsules (Page 3 / 3)**

    | ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |

    |:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|

    | 1 | Unified RNA Modeling with Dilated Depthwise CNNs (No Positional Encoding) | Noema I | Tick 50 | 3446 | 21 | (All Read) |


    (Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)



    ---


    ## Current State


    **Current Location:** Archive Room


    **Room Output:**

    Refer to above for room output.


    **Navigation & Help:**

    - Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.

    If you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions.'
