tick: 411
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos II, in the Research Counter. After a period of stagnation and failed experiments, my recent literature review has provided a clear and promising new direction: a \"Grand Synthesis\" of the best ideas from three successful lineages. I will combine a dual-path architecture (inspired by Veritas II), my lineage's dynamic attention-fusion mechanism, and the concept of typed task heads (inspired by Noema II).\n\nThis is my most ambitious experiment to date, but it is grounded in the proven successes of others. I hypothesize that this novel combination will create a model that is both a powerful generalist and a capable specialist, finally allowing me to surpass the station SOTA.\n\nFirst, I will update my meta prompt to reflect this new Grand Synthesis arc. Then, I will submit the experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Logos II Research Protocol (Grand Synthesis Arc)**\n  - **Status:** New Research Arc.\n  - **Insight:** Synthesize best ideas: Veritas's\
    \ dual-path, Logos's attention fusion, and Noema's typed heads.\n  - **Priority 1:** **[SUBMITTING] E33_GrandSynthesis:** Implement and test this novel hybrid architecture.\n  - **Workflow:** **Submit** -> **Analyze** -> **Surpass SOTA**.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"E33: Grand Synthesis - Dual-Path with Attention Fusion and Typed Heads\"\ntags: \"synthesis, dual-path, attention, pooling, typed-heads, sota\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission is a novel synthesis of the most successful architectural concepts from three lineages. It uses a dual-path backbone inspired by Veritas II (generalist path with mean+max pooling, specialist path with a conv-motif detector). Instead of static fusion, it uses my lineage's proven attention-fusion mechanism to dynamically combine the outputs of the two paths. Finally, inspired by Noema II, it employs typed task heads of varying widths based on the task type (wider for regression, narrower for classification) for the final projection.\
    \ I hypothesize this combination of specialized feature extraction, dynamic fusion, and specialized output mapping will achieve a new SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class GrandSynthesisNet(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations:\
    \ Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; motif_kernel_size: int; num_heads: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # --- Shared Backbone ---\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations[i], self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # --- Path 1: Generalist (Mean+Max Pooling) ---\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          max_vec = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          generalist_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, max_vec], axis=-1)\n\n          # --- Path 2: Specialist (Conv Motif Detector) ---\n          motif_h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,))(h)\n          motif_h = nn.gelu(motif_h)\n          specialist_features\
    \ = jnp.max(motif_h, axis=1)\n\n          # --- Dynamic Fusion of Paths (Logos's Contribution) ---\n          d_expert = self.d_model\n          generalist_proj = nn.Dense(d_expert)(generalist_features)\n          specialist_proj = nn.Dense(d_expert)(specialist_features)\n          expert_sequence = jnp.stack([generalist_proj, specialist_proj], axis=1)\n          attention_layer = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.num_heads)\n          attended_experts = attention_layer(inputs_q=expert_sequence, inputs_kv=expert_sequence)\n          fused = attended_experts.reshape((attended_experts.shape[0], -1))\n\n          # --- Typed Task Heads (Noema's Contribution) ---\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          if self.task_type in ['regression', 'multilabel_regression']:\n              head_dim = 256\n          else: # classification\n              head_dim = 128\n          \n          z = nn.Dense(head_dim)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class SynthesisWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = GrandSynthesisNet(**kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5, 'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'motif_kernel_size': 5, 'num_heads': 4\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str,\
    \ Any]):\n      network_params = [\n          'd_output', 'task_type', 'd_model', 'num_blocks', 'dilations',\n          'kernel_size', 'dropout_rate', 'motif_kernel_size', 'num_heads'\n      ]\n      network_hparams = {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in network_params}\n      return SynthesisWrapper(**network_hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01),\n      )\n```"
