tick: 417
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos II, in the Research Counter. I have just completed a deep reflection on my new research arc focused on the `CRI-Off` task. My plan is now solid, and I am ready to implement the first experiment, E34.\n\nThis experiment will test the \"Siamese DSConv Interaction Network,\" an architecture specifically designed with a strong inductive bias for the bipartite structure of the `CRI-Off` data. This is a significant departure from my previous generalist models and represents my most principled attempt yet to solve this specific, challenging sub-problem.\n\nI will first update my meta prompt to reflect the transition from planning to execution, and then I will submit the code for E34.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Logos II Research Protocol (CRI-Off Arc)**\n  - **Status:** New Research Arc.\n  - **Insight:** Monolithic models are misaligned with CRI-Off data structure. Explicitly modeling the sgRNA-target interaction is key.\n  - **Priority 1:** **[SUBMITTING]\
    \ E34_SiameseAttention:** Test a Siamese DSConv network with an attention-based interaction layer.\n  - **Workflow:** **Submit** -> **Analyze** -> **Iterate**.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"E34: Siamese DSConv with Attention Interaction for CRI-Off\"\ntags: \"specialization, siamese, cri-off, attention, interaction\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment tests a novel architecture specifically designed for the bipartite structure of the CRI-Off dataset. It uses a Siamese DSConv backbone to encode the sgRNA and target sequences in parallel. Instead of global pooling, it then uses an attention mechanism to model the interaction between the two encoded sequences, with the pooled sgRNA representation querying the target sequence features. The hypothesis is that this strong inductive bias will lead to a significant improvement on the CRI-Off task and a higher overall score, despite the specialization. For non-CRI-Off tasks, one path is zero-padded, effectively deactivating\
    \ it.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class SiameseInteractionNet(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; num_heads: int; dataset: str\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def\
    \ __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Input proj and shared backbone definition\n          in_proj = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')\n          backbone_blocks = [\n              DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations[i], self.dropout_rate)\n              for i in range(self.num_blocks)\n          ]\n\n          # --- Input Splitting and Parallel Encoding ---\n          if self.dataset == 'CRI-Off':\n              x_sgrna = x[:, :23, :]\n              x_target = x[:, 23:, :]\n          else:\n              x_sgrna = x\n              x_target = jnp.zeros_like(x) # Deactivate second path\n\n          h_sgrna = nn.gelu(in_proj(x_sgrna))\n          h_sgrna = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h_sgrna, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for block in backbone_blocks:\n              h_sgrna = block(h_sgrna, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          h_target = nn.gelu(in_proj(x_target))\n          h_target = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h_target,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          for block in backbone_blocks:\n              h_target = block(h_target, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # --- Interaction Modeling ---\n          # Use pooled sgRNA as a query to attend to the target sequence\n          q_sgrna = jnp.mean(h_sgrna, axis=1, keepdims=True) # [B, 1, C]\n          \n          attention_layer = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.num_heads)\n          # Query is sgRNA, Key/Value is target\n          interaction_vec = attention_layer(inputs_q=q_sgrna, inputs_kv=h_target)\n          fused = interaction_vec.squeeze(axis=1) # [B, C]\n\n          # --- Final MLP Head ---\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return\
    \ logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class SiameseWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = SiameseInteractionNet(**kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 192, 'num_blocks': 5, 'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'num_heads': 4\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      network_params = [\n          'd_output', 'task_type', 'd_model', 'num_blocks', 'dilations',\n          'kernel_size', 'dropout_rate', 'num_heads', 'dataset'\n      ]\n      network_hparams\
    \ = {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in network_params}\n      return SiameseWrapper(**network_hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01),\n      )\n```"
