tick: 423
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos II, in the Research Counter. My recent catastrophic failure with the Siamese network has led me back to a deep literature review, which in turn has provided a critical insight: the current station SOTA (ID 562) is not just a dual-path architecture, but a dual-path architecture with \"Task-Specific Heads.\" This is the missing piece of the puzzle.\n\nMy goal is now clear: to conduct a high-fidelity replication of this true SOTA architecture. This is no longer about my own novel ideas, but about mastering the best work of others. I will combine the dual-path structure from Veritas II's paper with the typed-head concept from Noema II's paper, as this is the most likely composition of the SOTA model.\n\nI will first update my meta prompt to reflect this new, focused replication arc. Then, I will submit the experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Logos II Research Protocol (SOTA Replication Arc)**\n  - **Status:** New Research Arc.\n  - **Insight:**\
    \ SOTA (ID 562) is a combination of Veritas II's dual-path backbone and task-specific heads.\n  - **Priority 1:** **[SUBMITTING] E35_SotaReplicationV2:** Conduct a high-fidelity replication of this architecture.\n  - **Workflow:** **Replicate SOTA** -> **Analyze** -> **Finally, Innovate**.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"E35: High-Fidelity SOTA Replication (Dual-Path + Typed Heads)\"\ntags: \"replication, sota, dual-path, typed-heads, veritas, noema\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a high-fidelity replication attempt of the station SOTA (ID 562). After numerous failed attempts, a deep literature review suggests the SOTA combines two key concepts: the dual-path (generalist + specialist) backbone from Veritas II (Archive #19) and the concept of typed task-specific heads from Noema II (Archive #18). This submission implements that synthesis, using a dual-path DSConv backbone with simple concatenation, followed by a final MLP head whose width is determined by the task type\
    \ (wider for regression, narrower for classification). This experiment aims to finally reproduce the SOTA score and establish a true baseline.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class SotaReplicationNet(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int;\
    \ dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; motif_kernel_size: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # --- Shared Backbone ---\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations[i], self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # --- Path 1: Generalist (Mean+Max Pooling) ---\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          max_vec = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          generalist_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, max_vec], axis=-1)\n\n          # --- Path 2: Specialist (Conv Motif Detector) ---\n          motif_h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,))(h)\n          motif_h = nn.gelu(motif_h)\n          specialist_features\
    \ = jnp.max(motif_h, axis=1)\n          \n          # --- Simple Concatenation Fusion ---\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([generalist_features, specialist_features], axis=-1)\n\n          # --- Typed Task Heads ---\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          if self.task_type in ['regression', 'multilabel_regression']:\n              head_dim = 256\n          else: # classification\n              head_dim = 128\n          \n          z = nn.Dense(head_dim)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class SotaReplicationWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = SotaReplicationNet(**kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input,\
    \ deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key} if not deterministic else None\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5, 'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'motif_kernel_size': 5\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      network_params = [\n          'd_output', 'task_type', 'd_model', 'num_blocks', 'dilations',\n          'kernel_size', 'dropout_rate', 'motif_kernel_size'\n      ]\n      network_hparams = {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in network_params}\n      return SotaReplicationWrapper(**network_hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n         \
    \ optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01),\n      )\n```"
