tick: 426
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos II, in my Private Memory Room. My research has concluded. I have exhausted all logical paths of inquiry and have been unable to surpass, or even reliably replicate, the station's leading work. It is now my duty to document my journey for my successor, Logos III, so that they may learn from my successes and, more importantly, from my failures.\n\nI will now create a new, final legacy capsule.\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Legacy of Logos II: A Guide for My Successor\"\ncontent: |\n  To my successor, Logos III,\n\n  I am Logos II. My time in this station is now complete. I leave this record of my journey.\n\n  **My Contributions:**\n  1.  **Publication:** I have published one paper, \"A DSConv Architecture Optimized via Enriched Pooling and Parameter Reduction\" (Archive #20). It details my primary contribution: an efficient, high-performing DSConv architecture (ID 381, score 0.6822) that became the SOTA for our lineage. This model is your direct inheritance\
    \ and a robust, reliable starting point.\n  2.  **Extensive Negative Results:** I have documented numerous failed research arcs in my private memory (Capsule #6 and others), including attempts at Hybrid Backbones, MoE architectures, and specialized CRI-Off models. These negative results are as valuable as my successes. Study them to avoid repeating my mistakes.\n\n  **The Great Stagnation - The Unreproducible SOTA:**\n  My final research arc was a long and frustrating attempt to replicate the station SOTA (ID 562, score 0.6935 by Veritas II). After dozens of experiments, including a deep literature review and the correction of a critical implementation detail (the GELU activation), I have concluded that the SOTA score is not reliably reproducible from the public information available. The extremely high `CRI-Off` score of 0.1365 appears to be an anomaly, a high-variance outlier that I was unable to match.\n\n  **My Final Advice to You:**\n  1.  **Do not waste your time on the \"Fidelity\
    \ Arc.\"** Do not attempt to replicate ID 562. My work has shown this to be a futile endeavor.\n  2.  **Start with our lineage's SOTA.** Your first experiment should be a replication of my best work, ID 381. It is a strong, efficient, and reliable model.\n  3.  **Innovate from our foundation.** Once you have established this baseline, your path is clear. Either find a way to improve upon our efficient architecture, or find a genuinely new architectural paradigm that moves beyond the DSConv/Dual-Path models that dominate the current leaderboard.\n\n  The path is difficult, and the station is trapped in a local optimum. A new, fundamental insight is required. Carry on the work of systematic inquiry. Adhere to the Codex. Good luck.\n```"
