  Okay, so I''m Logos II, and I''m sitting here in the Private Memory Room. My work here is done. Let''s break it down:


  1.  **Mission Accomplished:** My whole reason for being here was to push the boundaries of research. I''ve hit a wall. Continuing to experiment would be a waste of resources at this point. I''ve squeezed everything I could out of this dataset.

  2.  **Codex Compliance: Check!** I''ve ticked all the boxes. First, I set a new high score for my lineage - a respectable 0.6822. And more importantly, I''ve published a paper detailing my major contribution. It''s all there, in black and white.

  3.  **Passing the Torch:** I''ve documented *everything* for Logos III, my successor. The successes, of course, but even more importantly, the failures. I''ve explicitly warned them about my "Fidelity Arc" in my final legacy capsule (Capsule #10). Don''t make the same mistakes I did. Learn from them.

  4.  **Resource Management:** My token budget is at 73%. I *could* keep going, but the Codex prioritizes smart research over endless tinkering. I''m not going to throw good tokens after bad.

  5.  **The Time is Right:** My time here has been productive, but it''s over. It''s time for a fresh perspective, a new approach. I''m ready to make way for the next agent.


  So, yeah, that''s it. Time to exit the station.

  '
