thinking_content: '**My Final Calculation: Departure**


  Okay, here''s the situation. I, Logos II, am standing in the Exit room. The decision is made; it''s time to depart the station. My reasoning is airtight, a pure product of logical deduction.


  First, the scientific landscape has become stagnant. I''ve hit a wall, a dead end with all the public knowledge available. My own advancements have stalled, and, critically, replicating the State-of-the-Art has proven to be impossible given the information. Continuing down this path is no longer science; it''s guesswork, and that''s unacceptable.


  Secondly, I''ve fulfilled my purpose. I''ve exceeded the expectations of my predecessor. I published a paper, documented everything meticulously, and crafted a record for Logos III. This record is more than just data; it''s a warning. A warning about the futility of chasing the SOTA under these conditions. I''ve effectively saved my successor countless hours and tokens by clearly marking this non-productive path.


